7
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.600
<i>We are in Kam Tin. requesting backup.</i>

8
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.720
<i>An EU vehicle is attacked.
We need an ambulance.</i>

9
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>Around 15 male suspects here.</i>

10
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.120
<i>heavily armed. Requesting reinforcement.</i>

11
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.120
<i>On 27 July 2017.</i>

12
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.960
<i>I received an order from Central Control.</i>

13
00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.040
<i>saying that one
of the EU vehicles was attacked.</i>

14
00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.760
<i>And the attackers</i>

15
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.840
<i>were the gangsters we've been pursuing.</i>

16
00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:31.280
<i>Open fire!</i>

17
00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.360
<i>Three in front!</i>

18
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.280
<i>Suppress fire!</i>

19
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.360
<i>Go! Go!</i>

20
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.120
Take cover!

21
00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.480
<i>Officer Lee. One front left.</i>

22
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.760
<i>Man down. Cover!</i>

23
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:57.840
<i>Ten in Zone B.</i>

24
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.640
We're under heavy fire!

25
00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:04.600
One fella is injured.

26
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:05.880
<i>Cover Officer Fok.</i>

27
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.520
Officer Fok. Cover me.

28
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.560
Go to hell!

29
00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.400
<i>Eight more in Zone B.</i>

30
00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:40.560
<i>All round defense.</i>

31
00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.760
Hold on.

32
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.320
<i>Officer Fok. Watch out above!</i>

33
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.800
Stoppage! Guard!

34
00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.160
Out of the way! Bomb!

35
00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.480
As you saw.

36
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.720
what was the first defendant

37
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.640
doing at the scene?

38
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.640
I saw Officer Leung May-yee

39
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.000
chasing the first defendant.
Cheung Man-bing.

40
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.880
Don't run! Stop!

41
00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:30.680
<i>I saw the first defendant
escaping through the back door.</i>

42
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.600
So. I chased him.

43
00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.040
When you were chasing my client.

44
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.720
performing your duties.
did you carry your warrant card?

45
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.760
<i>It was an emergency.</i>

46
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.280
I dropped my warrant card.

47
00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.800
So. you failed to establish
your identity as a police officer.

48
00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.640
I certainly did not know
she was a police officer.

49
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.600
I heard gunshots. then a crazy woman

50
00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.240
rushed up trying to attack me.

51
00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.080
<i>At that time. Officer Leung</i>

52
00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.920
was behind him. trying

53
00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:00.856
to subdue the first defendant.
Cheung Man-bing.

54
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.840
In other words. my client

55
00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:04.736
- was attacked by her from behind.
- I absolutely disagree.

56
00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.560
He was forced to act in self-defense
and caused the accident.

57
00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.480
Officer Leung

58
00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.960
reasonably attempted

59
00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.480
to subdue the first defendant.
Cheung Man-bing.

60
00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.800
Cheung Man-bing intended to resist arrest.

61
00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.240
Go to hell.

62
00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:26.760
<i>The prosecution points out</i>

63
00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.000
<i>that you were unreasonably
at a deserted ruin.</i>

64
00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.080
How do you explain it?

65
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.040
I wanted to film something supernatural

66
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.400
for my YouTube channel.

67
00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.840
We didn't find any photographic
equipment at the crime scene.

68
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.920
The defendant is giving a false testimony

69
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.456
and is in flagrant contempt of court.

70
00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:43.920
<i>Nowadays. a mobile phone</i>

71
00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.600
<i>can film many things.</i>

72
00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.760
The prosecution's accusations
are unreasonable.

73
00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.240
<i>Ten gangsters were arrested.</i>

74
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.800
<i>All of them denied knowing my client.</i>

75
00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.120
It is sufficient to prove

76
00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.680
that my client is not related
to this case at all.

77
00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.056
Who will testify against their own boss?
Are you kidding me?

78
00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.080
Silence.

79
00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:01.280
Your Honor.

80
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.960
They are likely to collude and lie.

81
00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.296
Their testimonies are unreliable.

82
00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:09.080
The fact is that after
the police's forensic search.

83
00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.960
the scene and weapons

84
00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.400
contained no fingerprints
or DNA of my client.

85
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.320
The prosecution has made
accusations against my client

86
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.360
without any evidence or witnesses.

87
00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:20.616
which are deemed as defamation.

88
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.680
I must remind the jury

89
00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.520
that even if you suspect my client's
presence was unreasonable.

90
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.160
the benefit of doubt
should go to the defendant.

91
00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.336
I earnestly request that you
pronounce my client innocent

92
00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.720
because it is the only reasonable verdict.

93
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:37.280
Your Honor. I request a reopening
of the prosecution's case

94
00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.760
and the summoning of new witnesses.

95
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.120
On what basis?

96
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.800
You should know the law.

97
00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.200
Since the prosecution is not able

98
00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.200
to prove guilt beyond a reasonable doubt.

99
00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.480
and the jury reached a majority verdict.

100
00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:53.040
I hereby declare
that the defendant. Cheung Man-bing.

101
00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.440
is not guilty on all three charges.
possession of firearms.

102
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.560
assaulting a police officer.
and resisting arrest.

103
00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.800
and be released by the court.

104
00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:03.680
<i>Law enforcement is just
the beginning of the legal process.</i>

105
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.200
<i>When there are any small cracks.</i>

106
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.360
<i>we lose justice.</i>

107
00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.280
Get off.

108
00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:31.800
Move.

109
00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.040
Let's go.

110
00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:14.840
Officer Fok.

111
00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.160
All the best.

112
00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.480
Just a change of scenery.

113
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.120
Stick to your post.

114
00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.040
Stick to our post.

115
00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.320
AFTER A JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY
A HEROIC COP CAUGHT THREE ROBBERS

116
00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.280
SEVEN YEARS LATER

117
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:06.696
<i>The female defendant
stabbed the victim over 20 times.</i>

118
00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:08.240
Most of the stabs hit bone.

119
00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.600
How will you deal with it?

120
00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:12.360
She murdered him.
then remained at the crime scene.

121
00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.496
She admitted she wanted
to kill the victim for a long time.

122
00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.456
The evidence is conclusive.
Charge her with murder.

123
00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.880
However. we need to consider

124
00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:20.520
the crime scene was the victim's home.

125
00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.040
The female defendant picked up

126
00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.680
the fruit knife by chance.

127
00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.800
It was not premeditated.

128
00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.456
Charging her with murder might not work.

129
00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:27.536
No fingerprints were found in the house.

130
00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:29.920
She intentionally cleaned up the scene.

131
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.800
then waited for the police to arrest her.

132
00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.160
Don't you think that's strange?

133
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.640
Mr. Fok.

134
00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.360
You are an experienced HK police officer

135
00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:39.120
who transferred to assist us at the DOJ.

136
00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.800
You must have some insights.

137
00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.160
Just a career move.

138
00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.760
Let's investigate together.

139
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.440
I have another viewpoint.

140
00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.400
Most of the fatal injuries
were on the left side.

141
00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.520
Like this…

142
00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.720
But the suspect is left-handed.

143
00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:03.400
She would have had to use
a backhand. like this.

144
00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.640
It is not impossible.
but it would be difficult.

145
00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.320
Keep in mind.
the victim was a 200-pound man.

146
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.400
stronger than Benny.

147
00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:12.440
- Benny.
- Yes.

148
00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.440
Please help me to demonstrate.

149
00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.280
- Maggie. right?
- Yes. Hello.

150
00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:20.960
First. try to struggle with each other.

151
00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.600
- Try to stab Benny. Maggie.
- Okay!

152
00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.040
- Come on!
- Here I come.

153
00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.840
- Come on.
- More force.

154
00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:26.800
- Okay. Thank you.
- Hey!

155
00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:27.920
Thank you…

156
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.080
So. as you can see.

157
00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.440
a slim woman.

158
00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:34.160
weighing around 90 pounds.

159
00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.000
found it difficult to stab a 200-pound man

160
00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.880
who worked out regularly.

161
00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:40.280
like this.

162
00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.360
In other words.

163
00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.800
the murderer is likely someone else.

164
00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.160
It's my opinion.

165
00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.720
We have different opinions.
How about we make a bet?

166
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.080
- $500 for each.
- Sure.

167
00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.120
How about we bet beer instead?

168
00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:54.640
If I lose. my treat.

169
00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.720
- Okay.
- Sure.

170
00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:57.560
If you win. our treat.

171
00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.360
- Okay.
- Deal.

172
00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:01.640
Mr. Fok.

173
00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:02.560
Yes?

174
00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:04.440
- My name is Bao Ding.
- Hello.

175
00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.160
I'm the Pupil Master here.
I take care of all the newcomers.

176
00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.640
- Nice to meet you.
- I'll assist you in the first few cases.

177
00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.720
If you need anything. please let me know.

178
00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.200
Police are responsible for arrests.

179
00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:15.016
We. the DOJ.
are responsible for prosecuting

180
00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.360
and convicting the arrested suspects.

181
00:11:17.440 --> 00:11:18.800
This is your first case.

182
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.280
<i>Earlier this year.
Customs received a tip-off.</i>

183
00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:26.640
<i>It is said that someone send a parcel</i>

184
00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.800
<i>to import
one kilograms of cocaine from Brazil.</i>

185
00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.480
<i>So. the police ambushed</i>

186
00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.216
<i>and traced it to the home
of the first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.</i>

187
00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.920
<i>They arrested him
when he received the parcel.</i>

188
00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:40.680
Coming.

189
00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:47.800
- Are you Ma Ka-kit?
- Yes. I am.

190
00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:48.880
Sign here.

191
00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:52.160
FROM BRAZIL TO MA KA-KIT. HONG KONG

192
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.720
Police. This is my warrant card.

193
00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.440
We suspect drugs in your parcel.

194
00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.080
- Kit!
- Stop!

195
00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.760
Don't run!

196
00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.800
I've got nothing to do with this!

197
00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.680
I don't know anything.

198
00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:09.120
- Kit!
- There are drugs inside. sir.

199
00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.720
This parcel isn't mine.
I only lent someone my address.

200
00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.080
<i>After being arrested. Ma Ka-kit insisted</i>

201
00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.960
<i>that he only lent his address</i>

202
00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.480
<i>to the second defendant. Chan Kwok-wing.</i>

203
00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.520
<i>And the police actually found drugs
at Chan Kwok-wing's home.</i>

204
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:22.520
I want a lawyer.

205
00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.080
<i>The culprit was caught red-handed.</i>

206
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.680
There is no case.

207
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.800
However. after three months of remand.

208
00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.256
Ma Ka-kit suddenly reversed his testimony.

209
00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.561
claiming that he never lent
his address to Chan Kwok-wing.

210
00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:35.040
- What do you think?
- Ma Ka-kit has no criminal record.

211
00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.880
but his testimony is inconsistent.
That means he's lying.

212
00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.616
Chan Kwok-wing
has a drug possession record.

213
00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:41.240
and drugs were found at his home.

214
00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.800
Let's charge both of them.
Both of them are suspects.

215
00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:44.896
Let's see how the defense reacts.

216
00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.320
If you are planning anything.

217
00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:50.520
you need Prosecutor Yeung's approval.
That's the rule. Please follow it.

218
00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.240
Understood. Thank you.

219
00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:54.360
And about the beer bet…

220
00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.120
It's good to be confident.

221
00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.240
Mr. Bao…

222
00:12:58.600 --> 00:12:59.600
I love beer.

223
00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.120
You were caught red-handed in this case.

224
00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.920
It's difficult to avoid conviction.
I suggest you plead guilty

225
00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:15.896
because pleading guilty now
can reduce your sentence by one-third.

226
00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.640
I just lent my address
to someone for $1.000.

227
00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:19.960
I didn't know it's about drugs.

228
00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.080
Do I have to go to jail?

229
00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:23.320
Kit.

230
00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.920
We all believe you are innocent.

231
00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:29.360
but there's no evidence to prove
that Chan Kwok-wing used your address.

232
00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.640
If we lose the trial.

233
00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:33.440
we will appeal.

234
00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:35.840
If we win.
the Department of Justice will appeal.

235
00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.320
Each appeal requires scheduling.

236
00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:41.080
which means you will wait
endlessly in prison.

237
00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:45.240
Barrister Li's advice is the best
and the quickest way to get you out.

238
00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:47.600
If Kit pleads guilty.

239
00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.680
can we proceed to the trial immediately
without him going to prison?

240
00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.960
Actually. there are still many procedures
and formalities before the trial.

241
00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.560
and Chan Kwok-wing's lawyer
will also take action.

242
00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.600
You're Chan Kwok-wing. right?

243
00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:01.560
Now that the police
found drugs in your house

244
00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:04.440
and Ma Ka-kit has implicated you.

245
00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:07.680
saying that you used his address
to receive the parcel.

246
00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:12.320
the DOJ may charge you with conspiracy
to drug trafficking and possession.

247
00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.160
How can I work with you?

248
00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:17.320
First. we need to convince the police

249
00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:20.120
that Kit will change his plea to guilty.

250
00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.560
The police will then hand over
the documents to the DOJ.

251
00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:23.840
CONFESSION REPORT MA KA-KIT

252
00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.880
<i>The DOJ will propose</i>

253
00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:28.320
<i>a court mention after review.</i>

254
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:30.376
<i>The court will schedule
the trial as soon as possible.</i>

255
00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:32.400
<i>for Kit to appeal for leniency.</i>

256
00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:34.720
<i>Due to the large number of cases
the court has to handle.</i>

257
00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:37.696
<i>the later you decide to plead guilty.
the longer you will have to wait.</i>

258
00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.200
<i>But if Kit pleads guilty earlier.</i>

259
00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:43.040
<i>we can immediately schedule
the case in the High Court</i>

260
00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.880
<i>for him to appear to seek leniency.</i>

261
00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.520
CONFESSION REPORT MA KA-KIT

262
00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:55.040
Don't say I didn't remind you.

263
00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.040
When you were a cop.
you worshipped Lord Guan.

264
00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.696
Now you're in the DOJ.
you should worship Prosecutor Yeung.

265
00:14:58.720 --> 00:14:59.880
Remember that.

266
00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:04.560
Hello. Mr. Bao.

267
00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:06.360
Hello. You are?

268
00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:08.480
I am the lawyer representing
Ma Ka-kit. Li Sze-man.

269
00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:10.760
Is it possible to discuss
a plea agreement?

270
00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:11.680
The conditions?

271
00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.200
My client will admit to drug trafficking.

272
00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.480
The only condition is that
the prosecution must withdraw

273
00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.080
the conspiracy to drug trafficking
charge against Chan Kwok-wing.

274
00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.336
You are the lawyer for the first defendant

275
00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:24.520
and you want to withdraw
the charge against the second defendant?

276
00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:26.480
- This doesn't make sense.
- Ma Ka-kit changed

277
00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.920
his testimony because he felt guilty.

278
00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.440
stating that it has nothing to do
with Chan Kwok-wing.

279
00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:32.896
He didn't want to wrong
an innocent person.

280
00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.456
Chan Kwok-wing. the second defendant.
has a drug possession record.

281
00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:37.136
while the first defendant
has a clear record.

282
00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:39.616
It is fair to release the first defendant
but not the second defendant.

283
00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.400
Conspiracy will result
in a more severe punishment.

284
00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:44.216
Excluding conspiracy
with the second defendant

285
00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.000
is in my client's best interest.

286
00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.800
Sorry. I don't accept it.

287
00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:48.880
Shirley.

288
00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:50.616
- Prosecutor Yeung.
- Good morning.

289
00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:51.640
Morning.

290
00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:54.240
Plea bargaining is great.

291
00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.696
The defendant recognized his mistake
and pleaded guilty.

292
00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.560
saving us time and taxpayers' money.

293
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.200
- I agree.
- Thank you.

294
00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.320
You're welcome.

295
00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:06.200
- Hello. Good morning.
- Mr. Yeung.

296
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.640
This is the new prosecutor. Fok Chi-ho.

297
00:16:08.720 --> 00:16:09.480
- Hi. Mr. Fok.
- Hi.

298
00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:10.640
- Welcome.
- Nice to meet you.

299
00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:14.240
We will go through
the court procedures later…

300
00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.720
And that will settle the case.

301
00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:16.880
Thank you.

302
00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.320
- Prosecutor Yeung.
- Yes?

303
00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.160
Why not charge the second defendant?

304
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.856
It doesn't comply
with the Prosecution Code.

305
00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:27.360
The first defendant's testimony
consistently emphasized

306
00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.376
that the second defendant
is not related to the case.

307
00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.480
- So. I don't want to waste time.
- A waste of time?

308
00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:33.680
This is our duty. Prosecution.

309
00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.320
trial.

310
00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:37.680
finding the truth. and conviction.

311
00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.040
The Department of Justice's principle
has always been

312
00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.360
to charge with evidence
and to release if no evidence.

313
00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:46.320
Firstly. if the first defendant
admits to drug trafficking.

314
00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.560
we can charge the second defendant

315
00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.160
with drug possession.

316
00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:53.520
That means both individuals
who have committed a crime

317
00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.760
will go to prison.

318
00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.320
What more do you want?

319
00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.560
Your case involves
drug trafficking through mail.

320
00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.880
So. strictly speaking.

321
00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:06.920
whether others were involved
in drug trafficking is irrelevant to you.

322
00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.400
As a prosecutor.
you should understand that.

323
00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.640
It's almost ten o'clock.

324
00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:12.840
Okay. Court.

325
00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.480
Both of them plead guilty.
and both will be sentenced.

326
00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:19.960
Isn't that fair? What more do you want?

327
00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:29.480
Case number ESCC235/2023.

328
00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:33.160
The first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.
and the second defendant. Chan Kwok-wing.

329
00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.120
are suspected
of conspiracy to drug trafficking.

330
00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.080
Your Honor.

331
00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:38.441
The defense has reached
an agreement with the prosecution.

332
00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:41.360
My client. the first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.

333
00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.440
will admit to the charge
of drug trafficking.

334
00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:47.280
Does the prosecution agree?

335
00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.040
Your Honor.

336
00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.816
the DOJ will amend the charge
against the first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.

337
00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.800
to drug trafficking and withdraw
the conspiracy to drug trafficking against

338
00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.176
the second defendant. Chan Kwok-wing.

339
00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:03.720
but we will retain the charge
of drug possession against him.

340
00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:08.760
Ma Ka-kit.

341
00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:10.536
you are accused of having
one kilogram of cocaine

342
00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.800
mailed from overseas to your residence.

343
00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:16.080
You were arrested on the scene
while receiving the parcel.

344
00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:19.120
You are now charged with drug trafficking.

345
00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.520
How do you plead?

346
00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:25.360
I plead guilty.

347
00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.600
Can I have remission?

348
00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:29.320
Verdict will be made at the next hearing.

349
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.440
This judge pronounces

350
00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.336
the withdrawal of the charge
of the second defendant.

351
00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:35.320
Chan Kwok-wing. with
conspiracy to drug smuggling.

352
00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.720
His drug possession case
will be scheduled for trial.

353
00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:40.040
The first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.

354
00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.360
who admits to drug trafficking.

355
00:18:42.440 --> 00:18:45.320
will be referred to the High Court
for mitigation and sentencing.

356
00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:47.400
He will remain in custody.

357
00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:49.160
- Court adjourned.
- Court.

358
00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.080
Everyone wants to leave work early.

359
00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.960
just like prisoners
want to be released early.

360
00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:57.720
What's the problem?

361
00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:00.880
No problem at all.

362
00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.880
<i>You are in charge of Ma Ka-kit's case.</i>

363
00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.120
<i>You've interviewed him.</i>

364
00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:25.000
- What do you think?
- Initially. he resisted arrest.

365
00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.520
but was very cooperative
later at the police station.

366
00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.440
He kept saying it had
nothing to do with him

367
00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.000
and that he only lent his address.

368
00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.720
No criminal will admit guilt. right?

369
00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.880
I heard he had
a tragic background. though.

370
00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.640
How so?

371
00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:44.000
It hurts! That's not how you do it!

372
00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:45.920
You wasted everything!

373
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:47.760
Why can't you do anything right?

374
00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.240
You're so useless.

375
00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.920
- Please stop…
- Why can't you learn?

376
00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.680
<i>When he was young.
his father died from a drug overdose.</i>

377
00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.976
<i>Whenever his mother craved drugs.</i>

378
00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:01.320
<i>she would beat him. He ended up
in the hospital every time.</i>

379
00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.120
Bastard!

380
00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:07.320
Hey. don't…

381
00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:09.040
Stop…

382
00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.560
The most remarkable part is that

383
00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.560
his grandpa repaid his mother in kind

384
00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.520
and regained custody.

385
00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.280
so he wouldn't be sent to an orphanage.

386
00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.840
His mother deserved it.

387
00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.520
Tell me about it!

388
00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:32.200
Finally got you. bastard.

389
00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:33.920
Hey.

390
00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.880
You bastard. leave me alone.

391
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:00.440
Don't move!

392
00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:11.760
I'm a cop.

393
00:21:12.680 --> 00:21:13.520
You hear me?

394
00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:14.600
Come and help.

395
00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.760
My bro.

396
00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:20.560
Are you causing trouble here?

397
00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.136
You're under arrest on suspicion
of multiple drug cases. damn it!

398
00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.880
- Stop resisting.
- Grab your weapons.

399
00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.600
Hey!

400
00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.200
You bastard.

401
00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.280
Kill him!

402
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:40.960
Assaulting the police is a crime!

403
00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:33.960
Get him. Kill him.

404
00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:29.440
Hey! What are you doing?

405
00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:30.880
Help me!

406
00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:19.040
<i>You are surrounded by the police!</i>

407
00:24:19.120 --> 00:24:20.960
<i>Drop all weapons now!</i>

408
00:24:28.560 --> 00:24:29.560
Hold still!

409
00:24:33.160 --> 00:24:34.160
Don't move!

410
00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:37.920
Come down!

411
00:24:38.000 --> 00:24:39.000
Get down here!

412
00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:47.600
Are you okay?

413
00:24:49.280 --> 00:24:50.680
Wounds are just a mark of honor.

414
00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.256
Our superior's followed
these drug traffickers for a long time.

415
00:24:53.280 --> 00:24:55.040
- All thanks to you.
- You did great. too.

416
00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.080
Don't mention it.
Gotta get back to work now.

417
00:24:57.600 --> 00:24:58.600
Go!

418
00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:05.440
Hey.

419
00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:07.440
You take the lead now.

420
00:25:16.360 --> 00:25:18.320
Drug trafficker.
Piss here for your whole life.

421
00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:20.600
Go away.

422
00:25:23.280 --> 00:25:24.600
Watch out.

423
00:25:30.640 --> 00:25:33.120
<i>I know you're not used to prison life.</i>

424
00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:35.360
Try to rest as much as you can.

425
00:25:35.440 --> 00:25:37.320
Otherwise. you won't be able to hold on.

426
00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:39.800
I am fine.

427
00:25:39.880 --> 00:25:41.600
I can take care of myself.

428
00:25:42.320 --> 00:25:43.320
How about you?

429
00:25:44.120 --> 00:25:45.560
It's been so hot lately.

430
00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:47.280
Will you use the fan?

431
00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:49.080
Instead of saving on electricity?

432
00:25:49.160 --> 00:25:50.160
Tell me.

433
00:25:50.960 --> 00:25:52.400
Don't worry about me.

434
00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:54.680
When did I worry about you?

435
00:25:55.280 --> 00:25:56.880
I'm just asking you a few questions.

436
00:25:58.000 --> 00:26:01.240
You should go back to Shanghai
and find Uncle Bong.

437
00:26:01.320 --> 00:26:03.840
- Take a break.
- I could go any time.

438
00:26:03.920 --> 00:26:05.600
We can go together after you are released.

439
00:26:05.680 --> 00:26:07.120
It might be a long wait.

440
00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:09.160
Good conduct. be granted remission…

441
00:26:09.240 --> 00:26:11.200
You'll be released soon.

442
00:26:17.160 --> 00:26:18.680
It's not just a few years.

443
00:26:18.760 --> 00:26:19.960
What?

444
00:26:20.040 --> 00:26:22.040
Do you remember what Lawyer Li said?

445
00:26:22.120 --> 00:26:23.216
Pleading guilty can reduce your sentence.

446
00:26:23.240 --> 00:26:25.440
- Plus. you're a first-time offender.
- Someone in my cell

447
00:26:25.880 --> 00:26:28.320
got an eight-year sentence
for trafficking 200 grams of drugs.

448
00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:29.480
In my case.

449
00:26:29.560 --> 00:26:30.880
it's one kilogram.

450
00:26:34.080 --> 00:26:35.560
Is it calculated this way?

451
00:26:38.440 --> 00:26:39.960
When I get out.

452
00:26:41.560 --> 00:26:43.000
will you still be around?

453
00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:52.720
I talked to a legal aid lawyer.

454
00:26:52.800 --> 00:26:54.920
He said Kit's case can be won.

455
00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:57.480
He's preparing to help us
overturn the guilty plea.

456
00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:59.320
As long as you admit it was misleading.

457
00:26:59.400 --> 00:27:01.160
- Kit will be fine.
- We didn't mislead anyone.

458
00:27:01.840 --> 00:27:04.520
You know all the facts clearly.

459
00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:08.000
and there's even a signed confession
from Ma Ka-kit.

460
00:27:08.080 --> 00:27:09.720
You bastards.

461
00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:12.000
You knew that Kit was innocent.

462
00:27:12.080 --> 00:27:14.520
Yet you said we couldn't win
and advised him to plead guilty.

463
00:27:14.600 --> 00:27:15.976
claiming it would reduce the sentence.

464
00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:18.016
With good behavior credits
and deducting the holidays.

465
00:27:18.040 --> 00:27:19.296
he'll be out in around ten years.

466
00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:21.840
- I'm dead by that time!
- What're you doing!

467
00:27:28.720 --> 00:27:30.680
- Call the police.
- No need.

468
00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:32.360
You should go.

469
00:27:37.040 --> 00:27:38.040
Just go.

470
00:27:48.120 --> 00:27:49.960
There was a teenager

471
00:27:50.040 --> 00:27:52.360
wrongly accused of murder.

472
00:27:52.440 --> 00:27:56.040
There were doubts about his case.

473
00:27:56.760 --> 00:28:00.360
The boss said he must be prosecuted.

474
00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:06.600
The police officers said
they wouldn't investigate further.

475
00:28:07.320 --> 00:28:08.360
What did you do?

476
00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:11.800
Those British guys
gave up the investigation.

477
00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:18.000
so I went to find evidence on my own.

478
00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:19.800
In the end. that boy

479
00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:21.720
was acquitted. right?

480
00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:23.920
How did you know?

481
00:28:25.960 --> 00:28:27.240
You've talked about this case

482
00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:30.120
many times.

483
00:28:30.200 --> 00:28:33.240
It happened over 40 years ago.
You solved the case too.

484
00:28:36.560 --> 00:28:37.960
Your boss

485
00:28:39.960 --> 00:28:41.800
even gave you this medal.

486
00:28:46.200 --> 00:28:50.000
I thought this case
happened just five days ago.

487
00:28:50.640 --> 00:28:51.480
Anyway.

488
00:28:51.560 --> 00:28:54.960
law enforcers must stay true
to their mission.

489
00:28:55.040 --> 00:28:58.480
Even if one day you couldn't walk anymore.

490
00:28:58.560 --> 00:29:01.240
you wouldn't have any regrets.

491
00:29:01.320 --> 00:29:03.640
Maybe you just need to stop and rest.

492
00:29:04.800 --> 00:29:06.040
We've been talking for a while.

493
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:07.720
Do you still remember who I am?

494
00:29:18.560 --> 00:29:19.880
I'm hungry.

495
00:29:19.960 --> 00:29:22.240
Take me back to the retirement home.

496
00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.240
Okay.

497
00:29:37.040 --> 00:29:39.120
Why are you so slow?

498
00:29:39.200 --> 00:29:40.280
Back in the day.

499
00:29:40.360 --> 00:29:41.800
your dad…

500
00:29:42.400 --> 00:29:46.040
I saw some thieves robbing
a jewelry store and then got on a bus.

501
00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:48.880
I chased them all the way
from Mong Kok to Tsim Sha Tsui

502
00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:50.560
and finally caught them.

503
00:29:51.160 --> 00:29:52.880
Can you speed up?

504
00:29:53.480 --> 00:29:54.480
Can you handle it?

505
00:29:54.560 --> 00:29:55.840
Of course I can.

506
00:29:55.920 --> 00:29:57.120
Then hold on tight.

507
00:29:57.200 --> 00:29:58.440
Let's go.

508
00:30:00.960 --> 00:30:02.640
Are you okay? Is this fast enough?

509
00:30:04.480 --> 00:30:10.400
AFTER A JEWELRY STORE ROBBERY.
A HEROIC COP CAUGHT THREE ROBBERS

510
00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:12.640
Your Honor.

511
00:30:13.240 --> 00:30:15.800
the first defendant. my client Ma Ka-kit.

512
00:30:15.880 --> 00:30:17.560
has no understanding of the law.

513
00:30:17.640 --> 00:30:20.360
He only pleaded guilty because
he was misled by his former lawyer.

514
00:30:20.440 --> 00:30:22.000
This is extremely unfair.

515
00:30:22.080 --> 00:30:24.416
Therefore. I would like to apply
to overturn the guilty plea.

516
00:30:24.440 --> 00:30:26.440
Any remarks from the prosecution?

517
00:30:28.320 --> 00:30:29.640
I have no remarks. Your Honor.

518
00:30:35.800 --> 00:30:38.560
How could you offer no remarks
when they asked for a reverse plea?

519
00:30:39.720 --> 00:30:41.120
Are you intentionally making way?

520
00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:43.736
