but I would like to kindly remind you

778
00:42:01.120 --> 00:42:02.576
that our duty in criminal prosecution

779
00:42:02.600 --> 00:42:05.640
is not solely to ensure
the defendant's conviction

780
00:42:05.720 --> 00:42:08.800
but to present credible evidence

781
00:42:08.880 --> 00:42:12.200
of the crimes
we are presenting to the jury.

782
00:42:12.840 --> 00:42:14.640
Are you teaching me
how to do my job again?

783
00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:18.320
Should I take off my robe
and give it to you to wear?

784
00:42:18.400 --> 00:42:19.560
Or give you my judge's wig?

785
00:42:19.640 --> 00:42:20.880
Your Honor. what I mean is that

786
00:42:20.960 --> 00:42:24.000
you have already influenced the jury's
perception of the first defendant.

787
00:42:24.080 --> 00:42:26.560
So. I request that you
dismiss the jury immediately

788
00:42:26.640 --> 00:42:28.000
and order a retrial.

789
00:42:33.640 --> 00:42:34.720
Court is adjourned.

790
00:42:34.800 --> 00:42:35.840
Court.

791
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:44.760
I'm at a loss for words.

792
00:42:48.800 --> 00:42:50.280
Have some coffee.

793
00:42:51.160 --> 00:42:52.240
Thanks.

794
00:42:53.920 --> 00:42:56.520
You need to assess the situation.
It's like a police baton.

795
00:42:57.240 --> 00:42:59.600
Only extend when necessary
and retract when unnecessary.

796
00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:01.640
If you extend it all the time.
you'll suffer.

797
00:43:04.280 --> 00:43:06.560
I will watch your trial at 3:30.

798
00:43:06.640 --> 00:43:08.480
Shouldn't you stay for the verdict?

799
00:43:08.560 --> 00:43:09.960
Watch or not. nothing will change.

800
00:43:16.880 --> 00:43:19.360
We need to remember that
there must be a majority consensus

801
00:43:19.440 --> 00:43:21.120
for a ruling to be valid.

802
00:43:21.200 --> 00:43:23.640
It can be 7-0. 6-1. or 5-2.

803
00:43:23.720 --> 00:43:26.440
<i>If it's 4-3. there'll be a retrial.</i>

804
00:43:26.520 --> 00:43:27.520
Mr. Fok.

805
00:43:28.880 --> 00:43:31.240
The courtroom is truly a strange place.

806
00:43:31.320 --> 00:43:33.920
A bunch of legal professionals
struggling with each other.

807
00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:37.000
leaving it to seven laymen
to determine someone's fate.

808
00:43:37.080 --> 00:43:38.560
But you did well just now.

809
00:43:38.640 --> 00:43:40.120
Don't worry about the outcome.

810
00:43:40.200 --> 00:43:42.360
We all have the same goal.
and that is to help Kit.

811
00:43:42.440 --> 00:43:44.480
Mr. Au. cut the bullshit.

812
00:43:44.560 --> 00:43:46.160
Chief Juror.

813
00:43:46.240 --> 00:43:48.880
- Have you reached a verdict?
- Yes.

814
00:43:49.800 --> 00:43:51.320
Is the verdict unanimous?

815
00:43:51.400 --> 00:43:52.320
No.

816
00:43:52.400 --> 00:43:53.560
Is it a majority verdict?

817
00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:55.200
Yes.

818
00:43:55.240 --> 00:43:56.920
What was the vote result?

819
00:43:57.520 --> 00:43:58.920
5-2.

820
00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:01.640
Is the first defendant
guilty or not guilty?

821
00:44:01.720 --> 00:44:02.560
Guilty.

822
00:44:02.640 --> 00:44:05.120
Is the second defendant
guilty or not guilty?

823
00:44:06.080 --> 00:44:07.080
Not guilty.

824
00:44:08.160 --> 00:44:10.000
You are helping Chan Kwok-wing all along.

825
00:44:10.800 --> 00:44:12.920
You pushed Ma Ka-kit into hell.
didn't you?

826
00:44:16.160 --> 00:44:17.920
I will now pronounce the verdict.

827
00:44:18.560 --> 00:44:21.680
The first defendant. Ma Ka-kit.

828
00:44:21.760 --> 00:44:23.080
is guilty of drug trafficking.

829
00:44:23.680 --> 00:44:26.120
Due to his lack of remorse

830
00:44:26.200 --> 00:44:27.680
and the waste of court resources.

831
00:44:27.760 --> 00:44:29.000
he must be severely punished.

832
00:44:30.880 --> 00:44:32.600
He is sentenced to 27 years in prison.

833
00:44:33.360 --> 00:44:36.280
The second defendant. Chan Kwok-wing.
is acquitted and released.

834
00:44:40.120 --> 00:44:41.480
- Court is adjourned.
- Court.

835
00:44:45.040 --> 00:44:45.880
Kit.

836
00:44:45.960 --> 00:44:47.000
Stay strong.

837
00:44:47.880 --> 00:44:48.880
Kit.

838
00:44:50.200 --> 00:44:51.600
Stay strong.

839
00:44:51.680 --> 00:44:53.240
Don't worry.

840
00:44:53.320 --> 00:44:56.240
Grandpa won't let you
sit in prison for 27 years.

841
00:44:56.320 --> 00:44:59.520
I wouldn't be alive to see you released.

842
00:44:59.600 --> 00:45:01.440
Don't worry.

843
00:45:01.520 --> 00:45:02.600
I'll find a way.

844
00:45:40.600 --> 00:45:41.600
Sorry.

845
00:45:47.120 --> 00:45:48.640
Trust me. I will help you.

846
00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:52.440
I'll be in prison for 27 years.

847
00:45:56.960 --> 00:45:58.040
How will you help me?

848
00:46:09.240 --> 00:46:11.400
- Mr. Au. good morning.
- Morning.

849
00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:13.200
Madam Cheung.

850
00:46:13.280 --> 00:46:14.480
- Hi.
- Debbie.

851
00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:16.040
Hello. Man.

852
00:46:16.640 --> 00:46:17.800
Let me introduce you.

853
00:46:17.880 --> 00:46:19.976
Barrister Li.
She specializes in commercial fraud cases.

854
00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:21.360
She can help you.

855
00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:23.160
You can count on me.

856
00:46:23.840 --> 00:46:25.120
- KC.
- You're back?

857
00:46:25.200 --> 00:46:26.440
Let me go first.

858
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:28.520
I've taken on another civil case.

859
00:46:28.600 --> 00:46:30.320
It's a piece of cake for you.

860
00:46:30.400 --> 00:46:33.080
Last time. you mentioned
wanting a diamond over ten carats.

861
00:46:33.160 --> 00:46:34.960
I found a good one for you in Belgium.

862
00:46:35.040 --> 00:46:35.880
Flawless.

863
00:46:35.960 --> 00:46:38.080
Do you know what brought the client to us?

864
00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:40.520
It's their helplessness.

865
00:46:40.600 --> 00:46:43.080
Just like sick people
going to see a doctor.

866
00:46:43.160 --> 00:46:44.840
Guilty ones going
to church for confession.

867
00:46:44.920 --> 00:46:46.480
or having a villain hitting ritual.

868
00:46:46.560 --> 00:46:47.720
It's all the same.

869
00:46:48.840 --> 00:46:50.280
But you're different

870
00:46:50.840 --> 00:46:53.200
because you understand the law.
You're their savior.

871
00:47:01.840 --> 00:47:04.640
It's all thanks to your selfless efforts.

872
00:47:04.720 --> 00:47:06.040
working tirelessly at night.

873
00:47:06.120 --> 00:47:09.080
that the Department of Justice
can uphold the rule of law for society.

874
00:47:09.160 --> 00:47:13.520
But there are still
many crises and challenges.

875
00:47:13.600 --> 00:47:15.560
I hope everyone sticks to their posts

876
00:47:15.640 --> 00:47:18.200
and continues to uphold
justice for our citizens.

877
00:47:22.440 --> 00:47:25.680
Bao. thank you for taking care
of our colleagues.

878
00:47:25.760 --> 00:47:27.040
You're welcome. Director.

879
00:47:27.120 --> 00:47:29.440
- This is Fok Chi-ho.
- Hello. Director.

880
00:47:29.520 --> 00:47:31.240
Welcome
to the Department of Justice family.

881
00:47:32.440 --> 00:47:34.120
During your time in the police force.

882
00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:37.240
you were renowned
for fearlessly catching criminals

883
00:47:37.320 --> 00:47:38.680
and working diligently.

884
00:47:38.760 --> 00:47:42.320
We believe that with your experience
as a police officer.

885
00:47:42.400 --> 00:47:44.880
you can provide us
with a different perspective.

886
00:47:44.960 --> 00:47:47.680
Mr. Yeung here is the most experienced.

887
00:47:47.760 --> 00:47:48.800
If you have any questions.

888
00:47:48.880 --> 00:47:51.360
he can guide you appropriately.

889
00:47:51.440 --> 00:47:53.120
You should work together closely.

890
00:47:53.200 --> 00:47:54.080
Absolutely. I hope so.

891
00:47:54.160 --> 00:47:55.840
I will do my best to assist Mr. Fok.

892
00:47:55.920 --> 00:47:58.216
He's smart. Everything will be fine.
Rest assured. Director.

893
00:47:58.240 --> 00:47:59.160
I understand

894
00:47:59.240 --> 00:48:01.920
that Prosecutor Fok
still has doubts about your first case.

895
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:03.400
But as the prosecution.

896
00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:04.800
even if we see a problem.

897
00:48:04.880 --> 00:48:07.640
only the defense has the right to appeal.

898
00:48:07.720 --> 00:48:11.320
At this stage. there's not much
the Department of Justice can do.

899
00:48:11.400 --> 00:48:12.240
I see. Director.

900
00:48:12.320 --> 00:48:15.480
However. it's just a hypothesis.
let's say the defendant

901
00:48:16.440 --> 00:48:18.360
requests an appeal.

902
00:48:18.440 --> 00:48:20.040
I really hope that you. as Director.

903
00:48:20.120 --> 00:48:21.360
will examine this case.

904
00:48:21.440 --> 00:48:24.040
Mr. Fok. why are you so eager

905
00:48:24.120 --> 00:48:25.680
for the defendant to file an appeal?

906
00:48:26.360 --> 00:48:28.840
The court has already
made a clear judgment.

907
00:48:28.920 --> 00:48:31.440
I really want to know what the problem is.

908
00:48:31.520 --> 00:48:34.360
Or do you simply want to see
the DOJ lose a lawsuit?

909
00:48:35.760 --> 00:48:38.600
This kind of rational discussion
is part of your daily work.

910
00:48:38.680 --> 00:48:40.520
You can revisit it another day.

911
00:48:40.600 --> 00:48:43.600
But today. there's a crucial task
for us to complete.

912
00:48:47.520 --> 00:48:49.880
- Hello. George.
- Hi. Selina.

913
00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:51.800
- Selina.
- It's been a while.

914
00:48:51.880 --> 00:48:54.520
Do you remember? Next month.
our alumni association

915
00:48:54.600 --> 00:48:56.296
is holding a golf tournament.
You're on my team.

916
00:48:56.320 --> 00:48:57.816
Make sure you come early
for the photo shoot.

917
00:48:57.840 --> 00:48:59.480
Alright.

918
00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:01.320
Everyone. come over here.

919
00:49:01.400 --> 00:49:02.760
- Full house today.
- Yes.

920
00:49:03.400 --> 00:49:05.160
- Please have a seat.
- Grand Judge.

921
00:49:05.240 --> 00:49:06.640
- Take a seat.
- Mr. Yeung.

922
00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:08.000
- Grand Judge.
- Mr. Bao.

923
00:49:09.160 --> 00:49:10.960
- Grand Judge.
- Have a seat.

924
00:49:11.600 --> 00:49:12.920
Take a seat.

925
00:49:15.360 --> 00:49:18.360
Director. your subordinate
also calls me "Grand Judge".

926
00:49:18.440 --> 00:49:19.240
He doesn't know

927
00:49:19.320 --> 00:49:22.440
everyone present here
can call me "Grand Judge".

928
00:49:22.520 --> 00:49:24.200
except for you.

929
00:49:24.280 --> 00:49:25.880
Right. Mr. Yeung?

930
00:49:27.440 --> 00:49:29.280
Before 1997.

931
00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:34.000
all judges of the High Court and above
were called "Grand Judge".

932
00:49:34.080 --> 00:49:35.320
That's why they called me that.

933
00:49:35.400 --> 00:49:39.240
After 1997. they unified the title
to "Judge". without the"Grand".

934
00:49:39.320 --> 00:49:40.360
So.

935
00:49:40.440 --> 00:49:42.760
any friends I knew before 1997

936
00:49:42.840 --> 00:49:44.120
can still call me "Grand Judge".

937
00:49:44.160 --> 00:49:46.840
But as for you.

938
00:49:46.920 --> 00:49:48.680
it's not suitable. right?

939
00:49:48.760 --> 00:49:50.880
Thank you for going easy on him.

940
00:49:50.960 --> 00:49:52.160
I should thank you.

941
00:49:52.760 --> 00:49:54.520
Marco. pour the wine.

942
00:49:55.880 --> 00:49:57.120
Mr. Fok.

943
00:50:02.280 --> 00:50:03.280
Frankly.

944
00:50:04.600 --> 00:50:08.920
as a judge. I only consider three rules.

945
00:50:09.000 --> 00:50:10.680
There's no fourth.

946
00:50:11.200 --> 00:50:13.160
It's witnesses. physical evidence.

947
00:50:13.240 --> 00:50:15.280
and the jury's decision.

948
00:50:15.880 --> 00:50:16.960
Listen.

949
00:50:17.040 --> 00:50:17.960
Honestly.

950
00:50:18.040 --> 00:50:20.320
sometimes. one can't
always do as one like.

951
00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:22.240
I know the defendant is guilty.

952
00:50:22.320 --> 00:50:24.216
but if there's no evidence.
I have to let them go.

953
00:50:24.240 --> 00:50:25.160
Conversely.

954
00:50:25.240 --> 00:50:27.680
sometimes I know they're innocent.

955
00:50:27.760 --> 00:50:30.080
but if there's evidence.
I have to convict them.

956
00:50:30.160 --> 00:50:33.000
These are traditional rules.

957
00:50:33.080 --> 00:50:35.360
Inevitably. even as a "Grand Judge".

958
00:50:35.440 --> 00:50:37.440
I still have to follow the rules.

959
00:50:37.520 --> 00:50:40.520
There's no reason for you to ignore them
and do as you please. right?

960
00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:43.560
But this time. I understand.

961
00:50:43.640 --> 00:50:46.520
It's your first time working
for the Department of Justice.

962
00:50:46.600 --> 00:50:47.920
and you have no experience.

963
00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:49.520
I'll forgive you this time.

964
00:50:49.600 --> 00:50:50.640
Okay.

965
00:50:50.720 --> 00:50:52.560
Cut the chatter. Let's drink.

966
00:50:53.200 --> 00:50:57.240
This bottle of wine is extraordinary.
Parker gave it a score of 100.

967
00:50:57.320 --> 00:51:00.040
It's a 1992 Chateau Leblanc.

968
00:51:00.120 --> 00:51:02.800
Let's all try it.
I bought it at an auction in France.

969
00:51:03.440 --> 00:51:07.120
In 1982. this lady was abandoned
by her husband and got divorced.

970
00:51:07.200 --> 00:51:09.560
While stomping grapes and making wine.

971
00:51:09.640 --> 00:51:13.200
she cried the whole time.
Her tears fell into the grape juice.

972
00:51:13.280 --> 00:51:14.640
So. now. when you drink it.

973
00:51:14.720 --> 00:51:16.920
there's a taste of her sorrow.

974
00:51:17.000 --> 00:51:19.080
Let's all drink.
See if there's any taste of sadness.

975
00:51:26.120 --> 00:51:29.240
Mr. Fok. can you taste the sadness?

976
00:51:31.320 --> 00:51:32.920
This bottle of wine is expensive.

977
00:51:33.000 --> 00:51:34.160
Even a glass costs thousands.

978
00:51:34.200 --> 00:51:35.200
Yes.

979
00:51:37.120 --> 00:51:41.200
It's the monthly income
of a poor family in Hong Kong.

980
00:51:41.880 --> 00:51:44.920
Indeed. that's quite sad.

981
00:51:50.320 --> 00:51:53.400
I like your sense of humor.

982
00:51:53.480 --> 00:51:54.480
You're a smart guy.

983
00:52:14.160 --> 00:52:15.160
Uncle Ma.

984
00:52:16.680 --> 00:52:18.360
You sent my grandson to prison.

985
00:52:18.440 --> 00:52:20.480
- What do you want?
- I understand how you feel.

986
00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:23.280
Can you give me a few minutes?
I want to say something.

987
00:52:24.080 --> 00:52:26.560
There are many loopholes in this case.

988
00:52:26.640 --> 00:52:28.640
So. on behalf
of the Department of Justice.

989
00:52:28.720 --> 00:52:30.040
I apologize to you.

990
00:52:32.200 --> 00:52:34.680
Additionally. I want to remind you

991
00:52:35.640 --> 00:52:38.720
that as a citizen. you have the right
to exercise your civil rights

992
00:52:38.800 --> 00:52:41.320
- and file an appeal.
- I don't need your reminder.

993
00:52:41.400 --> 00:52:42.480
I already applied.

994
00:52:42.560 --> 00:52:43.760
Lawyer Cheng told me

995
00:52:43.840 --> 00:52:46.600
not to talk to anyone during this time.

996
00:52:46.680 --> 00:52:47.520
- Okay.
- Stop bothering me.

997
00:52:47.600 --> 00:52:49.160
I want you to believe

998
00:52:50.880 --> 00:52:53.160
- our society is lawful.
- Everyone pretends to be nice.

999
00:52:53.240 --> 00:52:55.080
I don't believe any of your nonsense.

1000
00:52:57.200 --> 00:52:59.520
I don't believe you hypocrites.

1001
00:52:59.600 --> 00:53:01.120
You're pretending to be the good guys.

1002
00:54:01.400 --> 00:54:03.400
Help! Help!

1003
00:54:14.200 --> 00:54:15.560
Help!

1004
00:55:04.880 --> 00:55:06.520
We've recorded Uncle Ma's statement.

1005
00:55:06.600 --> 00:55:09.320
Right after he filed his appeal.
he was attacked.

1006
00:55:09.400 --> 00:55:12.840
It was most likely
that paralegal and the lawyer.

1007
00:55:13.440 --> 00:55:15.536
We recently seized several
vehicles transporting drugs.

1008
00:55:15.560 --> 00:55:18.720
and your case is also
related to drug trafficking.

1009
00:55:18.800 --> 00:55:19.960
Be careful.

1010
00:55:27.320 --> 00:55:29.160
You really don't have to drive me home.

1011
00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:31.200
I can get home myself.

1012
00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:33.200
No worries. It's on my way.

1013
00:55:36.320 --> 00:55:38.440
It's messy here. Be careful.

1014
00:55:40.720 --> 00:55:42.520
Don't mind my humble abode.

1015
00:55:43.440 --> 00:55:44.600
Take a seat.

1016
00:55:46.480 --> 00:55:48.120
I'll open the window for fresh air.

1017
00:55:51.680 --> 00:55:52.920
I'll get you a cup of tea.

1018
00:55:55.480 --> 00:55:56.840
Damn.

1019
00:55:57.600 --> 00:55:59.200
It ran off again.

1020
00:55:59.720 --> 00:56:01.840
- Please have some tea.
- Thanks.

1021
00:56:09.560 --> 00:56:11.640
Whenever it rains outside.

1022
00:56:11.720 --> 00:56:13.240
it leaks here.

1023
00:56:13.320 --> 00:56:15.600
As the saying goes.
"Water is wealth." right?

1024
00:56:16.480 --> 00:56:18.560
It's fine. as long
as I won't starve to death.

1025
00:56:27.640 --> 00:56:29.080
Did your grandson draw all of these?

1026
00:56:29.160 --> 00:56:30.560
Yes. Kit drew them.

1027
00:56:30.640 --> 00:56:32.480
He loves drawing tall buildings.

1028
00:56:32.560 --> 00:56:34.936
He often tells me that he wants me
to live in a better place.

1029
00:56:34.960 --> 00:56:36.320
As soon as he turned 18.

1030
00:56:36.400 --> 00:56:38.320
he applied for public housing.

1031
00:56:38.400 --> 00:56:42.280
We were hoping to move
to public housing in a few years.

1032
00:56:49.400 --> 00:56:50.400
Uncle Ma.

1033
00:56:51.240 --> 00:56:52.840
How do you know Li Sze-man?

1034
00:56:53.560 --> 00:56:56.400
I was introduced by the owner
of the restaurant where Kit works.

1035
00:56:56.480 --> 00:56:58.200
I think his last name is Lau.

1036
00:56:59.240 --> 00:57:02.320
He knew Kit was hardworking.
so he referred a paralegal to him.

1037
00:57:02.400 --> 00:57:06.560
Then the paralegal introduced us
to the bitch who offered to help for free.

1038
00:57:06.640 --> 00:57:09.480
We're too poor to have a choice.

1039
00:57:09.560 --> 00:57:13.360
Just talking to a lawyer costs thousands.
How could I afford it?

1040
00:57:14.280 --> 00:57:16.680
You legal aid or DOJ folks.

1041
00:57:17.200 --> 00:57:19.560
all from the government. can't help us.

1042
00:57:20.560 --> 00:57:22.760
After all this chaos. you must be hungry.

1043
00:57:22.840 --> 00:57:24.040
Make yourself at home.

1044
00:57:24.120 --> 00:57:25.640
I'll make two bowls of noodles.

1045
00:57:25.720 --> 00:57:27.880
I didn't realize I was hungry
until you mentioned it.

1046
00:57:27.960 --> 00:57:29.040
Just a second.

1047
00:58:17.560 --> 00:58:19.600
Mr. Fok. everyone has left already.

1048
00:58:19.680 --> 00:58:21.720
Come. Let's have a drink
during Happy Hour.

1049
00:58:22.320 --> 00:58:24.000
I found new clues in the Ma Ka-kit case.

1050
00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:28.400
You realize
that there's no overtime. right?

1051
00:58:31.480 --> 00:58:33.360
<i>Ma Ka-kit's previous boss. Lau Siu-keung.</i>

1052
00:58:33.440 --> 00:58:34.920
<i>is a new lead in this case.</i>

1053
00:58:35.000 --> 00:58:36.040
<i>We need to find out</i>

1054
00:58:36.120 --> 00:58:38.360
<i>about his relationship
with Li Sze-man and Au Pak-man.</i>

1055
00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:39.920
<i>It's the only way to help Ma Ka-kit.</i>

1056
00:58:40.000 --> 00:58:41.680
According to our intelligence reports.

1057
00:58:41.760 --> 00:58:44.000
in recent years. Lau Siu-keung
opened many restaurants.

1058
00:58:44.080 --> 00:58:45.840
wine stores. and nightclubs.

1059
00:58:45.920 --> 00:58:47.800
<i>He appears to be a legitimate businessman.</i>

1060
00:58:47.880 --> 00:58:49.760
<i>Behind the scenes.
he works with triad leaders.</i>

1061
00:58:50.520 --> 00:58:53.920
<i>All his businesses are managed
by Au Pak-man's law firm.</i>

1062
00:58:54.680 --> 00:58:56.840
<i>Li Sze-man is really something.</i>

1063
00:58:56.920 --> 00:58:58.400
<i>She grew up in an orphanage.</i>

1064
00:58:58.480 --> 00:59:01.200
<i>and later. Au Pak-man paid
for her education in the United States.</i>

1065
00:59:01.280 --> 00:59:03.400
<i>where she also obtained a law license.</i>

1066
00:59:03.480 --> 00:59:05.440
<i>If I were her. I'd fall for him too.</i>

1067
00:59:05.520 --> 00:59:07.560
<i>I checked the DOJ internal records.</i>

1068
00:59:07.640 --> 00:59:09.280
<i>Au Pak-man got his early release</i>

1069
00:59:09.360 --> 00:59:10.840
<i>because Li Sze-man won his case.</i>

1070
00:59:16.720 --> 00:59:17.720
LUCKY SIX
12-1/20-1

1071
00:59:21.080 --> 00:59:22.360
Please conclude. Bao Ding.

1072
00:59:23.640 --> 00:59:25.000
Isn't it obvious?

1073
00:59:25.080 --> 00:59:26.760
They're the masterminds.

1074
00:59:27.840 --> 00:59:29.240
<i>Au Pak-man is so impressive.</i>

1075
00:59:29.320 --> 00:59:30.560
He's been in prison

1076
00:59:30.640 --> 00:59:33.840
for assault. extortion. money laundering.
drugs… Almost all crimes.

1077
00:59:33.920 --> 00:59:35.240
Yet he still works at a law firm.

1078
00:59:35.320 --> 00:59:36.440
That's ridiculous.

1079
00:59:36.520 --> 00:59:37.920
We can work this out.

1080
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:39.216
Dealing with the evidence is easy

1081
00:59:39.240 --> 00:59:41.160
because he wasn't caught red-handed.

1082
00:59:41.840 --> 00:59:42.680
- Yes.
- Au Pak Man.

1083
00:59:42.760 --> 00:59:43.816
- Get lost!
- Go jerk yourself!

1084
00:59:43.840 --> 00:59:44.880
<i>For money laundering.</i>

1085
00:59:44.960 --> 00:59:46.320
<i>I take a 20% cut.</i>

1086
00:59:46.400 --> 00:59:50.400
Whether it's 100 million or one billion.
I don't care. 20%. that's how it is.

1087
00:59:51.160 --> 00:59:54.320
<i>CSD officers said
he diligently studied law in prison.</i>

1088
00:59:54.400 --> 00:59:56.576
After being released. he continued
smuggling and trafficking drugs.

1089
00:59:56.600 --> 00:59:59.560
But he won all the cases by himself.

1090
00:59:59.640 --> 01:00:02.000
He also knows
many influential figures in prison.

1091
01:00:02.080 --> 01:00:04.240
We arrested one of them.

1092
01:00:04.320 --> 01:00:06.000
Sang. from Cambodia.

1093
01:00:06.080 --> 01:00:07.000
SANG'S RECORDS
IN CORRECTIONAL SERVICES DEPARTMENT

1094
01:00:07.080 --> 01:00:08.080
SANG'S FINGERPRINT

1095
01:00:23.680 --> 01:00:24.520
Cash out.

1096
01:00:24.600 --> 01:00:25.840
Let's go.

1097
01:00:42.600 --> 01:00:43.600
Keung.

1098
01:00:43.960 --> 01:00:45.840
I am in conflict with the God of the Year.

1099
01:00:45.920 --> 01:00:48.440
Some drug cars got busted.
The batch in the coconuts was seized.

1100
01:00:49.160 --> 01:00:50.600
We should lay low for a while.

1101
01:00:50.680 --> 01:00:51.680
Hold deliveries for now.

1102
01:00:52.240 --> 01:00:53.080
No deliveries?

1103
01:00:53.160 --> 01:00:55.360
The bosses will definitely throw a fit.

1104
01:00:55.440 --> 01:00:56.520
Throw a fit?

1105
01:00:56.600 --> 01:00:58.640
Let them. then.

1106
01:00:58.720 --> 01:01:01.920
If the goods are seized by the cops.
I would go crazy.

1107
01:01:03.920 --> 01:01:06.520
The incident with Uncle Ma
was because of you two. right?

1108
01:01:06.600 --> 01:01:07.920
You're so smart.

1109
01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:09.840
Nothing escapes you.

1110
01:01:10.360 --> 01:01:13.080
It could be either Tung or Sang.

1111
01:01:13.160 --> 01:01:14.920
Who else could it be?

1112
01:01:15.000 --> 01:01:16.440
That's why I always say.

1113
01:01:16.520 --> 01:01:17.760
brutes will be brutes.

1114
01:01:17.840 --> 01:01:18.920
They only use violence.

1115
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:20.080
Keung.

1116
01:01:21.680 --> 01:01:23.360
You're a smart guy.

1117
01:01:23.440 --> 01:01:24.840
civilized.

1118
01:01:25.480 --> 01:01:27.080
So. in the future. whatever you do.

1119
01:01:27.160 --> 01:01:29.920
don't be as foolish as they are.

1120
01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:31.560
- Okay?
- Understood. Boss.

1121
01:01:43.640 --> 01:01:44.520
Sang. take a seat.

1122
01:01:44.600 --> 01:01:45.640
Have a seat.

1123
01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:56.280
Your underling

1124
01:01:56.360 --> 01:01:58.320
stole my batch of coconuts.

1125
01:01:58.400 --> 01:02:00.560
causing me a loss of 50 million.

1126
01:02:01.680 --> 01:02:02.840
When will you compensate me?

1127
01:02:02.920 --> 01:02:05.480
You can only accuse him of stealing
if he's taken it for himself.

1128
01:02:06.120 --> 01:02:07.600
The police confiscated everything.

1129
01:02:07.680 --> 01:02:08.760
I want to compensate you.

1130
01:02:08.840 --> 01:02:10.680
but Man can't make any deliveries now.

1131
01:02:11.240 --> 01:02:12.400
Let's see what he has to say.

1132
01:02:13.640 --> 01:02:15.280
Personally. I think

1133
01:02:15.360 --> 01:02:17.656
if we make deliveries now.
it's like delivering to the cops.

1134
01:02:17.680 --> 01:02:19.320
The 50 million you lost.

1135
01:02:19.400 --> 01:02:20.520
I'll personally pay it back.

1136
01:02:21.640 --> 01:02:22.880
As for Tung.

1137
01:02:22.960 --> 01:02:25.360
I'll give you 30% off
on the next three batches.

1138
01:02:25.440 --> 01:02:27.440
- This way. everyone's satisfied.
- A wonderful deal.

1139
01:02:31.800 --> 01:02:33.920
You really think that money is everything?

1140
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:35.240
Sang.

1141
01:02:35.760 --> 01:02:37.200
I know what you want.

1142
01:02:48.200 --> 01:02:49.360
Let me go.

1143
01:02:49.440 --> 01:02:51.480
Tung. You're not
going to do this. are you?

1144
01:02:51.560 --> 01:02:54.320
I've followed you since I was a kid.
You'll do this to me?

1145
01:02:54.400 --> 01:02:55.400
Let me go!

1146
01:02:56.440 --> 01:02:57.440
You're crazy.

1147
01:02:57.520 --> 01:02:59.400
This time. my underling made a mistake.

1148
01:02:59.480 --> 01:03:00.800
I know what to do.

1149
01:03:00.880 --> 01:03:02.000
Man.

1150
01:03:03.360 --> 01:03:04.560
Give me a hand.

1151
01:03:07.000 --> 01:03:08.200
Will you do it or not?

1152
01:03:08.280 --> 01:03:09.680
Didn't you hear the boss. dumb-ass?

1153
01:03:09.760 --> 01:03:11.000
Hit him.

1154
01:03:11.080 --> 01:03:13.640
- Hit him.
- Do it!

1155
01:03:13.720 --> 01:03:15.000
Come on.

1156
01:03:20.000 --> 01:03:23.000
Sang. I didn't know the cocaine
in those coconuts belonged to you.

1157
01:03:23.080 --> 01:03:24.480
Please. give me a chance.

1158
01:03:24.560 --> 01:03:26.680
Tung. I know I was wrong.

1159
01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:29.080
Please help me plead with Sang.

1160
01:03:29.600 --> 01:03:30.760
I beg you…

1161
01:03:31.640 --> 01:03:32.840
Don't do this.

1162
01:03:45.840 --> 01:03:47.560
Wow. Do you really have to go this far?

1163
01:03:47.640 --> 01:03:48.840
Are you satisfied?

1164
01:03:53.320 --> 01:03:54.720
I never said I wasn't satisfied.

1165
01:03:55.400 --> 01:03:56.600
Take him to a doctor.

1166
01:04:01.400 --> 01:04:04.200
Make sure the goods reach us tomorrow.

1167
01:04:04.280 --> 01:04:05.760
Bosses…

1168
01:04:06.440 --> 01:04:08.320
It's not that I don't want to deliver.

1169
01:04:08.400 --> 01:04:09.760
I'm still involved in a case.

1170
01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:11.200
I'm being watched closely.

1171
01:04:13.480 --> 01:04:15.560
I'll handle your case.

1172
01:04:16.320 --> 01:04:18.720
Make sure you keep delivering.

1173
01:04:20.200 --> 01:04:21.320
You hear me?

1174
01:04:23.120 --> 01:04:24.120
Go.

1175
01:04:28.840 --> 01:04:30.200
I'm leaving now. Sang.

1176
01:04:31.960 --> 01:04:33.160
You bastard.

1177
01:04:33.680 --> 01:04:35.680
You're so brutal.
even with your own underlings.

1178
01:04:35.760 --> 01:04:36.760
That's how we do things.

1179
01:04:38.440 --> 01:04:39.760
If we don't scare him a little.

1180
01:04:40.600 --> 01:04:42.640
he won't deliver the goods.

1181
01:04:56.760 --> 01:04:58.200
Hello. Bao Ding.

1182
01:04:58.280 --> 01:04:59.440
I can't hear you.

1183
01:05:01.000 --> 01:05:02.880
It's noisy. Speak up.

1184
01:05:37.280 --> 01:05:38.520
You piece of shit.

1185
01:05:38.600 --> 01:05:40.176
You know it's my place. yet you do drugs?

1186
01:05:40.200 --> 01:05:42.200
Is your place more important than me?

1187
01:05:42.280 --> 01:05:43.800
Without me. you'd have died long ago.

1188
01:05:43.880 --> 01:05:45.200
Get the fuck out.

1189
01:05:45.280 --> 01:05:47.280
Now! Get out!

1190
01:05:51.360 --> 01:05:52.880
Stop playing big brother. you bastard.

1191
01:05:54.760 --> 01:05:55.600
I am your big brother. So what?

1192
01:05:55.680 --> 01:05:57.200
My last name is Chan.

1193
01:05:57.280 --> 01:05:59.920
- Your dad isn't my dad.
- But we share the same mom. don't we?

1194
01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:01.360
- Yes. so what?
- Get lost.

1195
01:06:02.760 --> 01:06:04.160
I'll leave once I've had enough.

1196
01:06:07.440 --> 01:06:08.280
- Stop!
- Bitch!

1197
01:06:08.360 --> 01:06:09.920
- Someone's here.
- Someone is filming us.

1198
01:06:11.920 --> 01:06:13.320
I've seen him in court.

1199
01:06:19.240 --> 01:06:20.240
Sorry.

1200
01:06:29.040 --> 01:06:30.040
What are you filming?

1201
01:06:33.720 --> 01:06:35.080
Give me your phone.

1202
01:06:39.320 --> 01:06:41.120
Hey! What's going on? Gang fight. huh?

1203
01:06:42.440 --> 01:06:43.440
I called the cops.

1204
01:06:47.800 --> 01:06:50.000
Took you long enough. Let's go.

1205
01:06:50.080 --> 01:06:51.720
I got what we need. Let's go.

1206
01:06:51.800 --> 01:06:52.840
Are you okay?

1207
01:06:52.920 --> 01:06:54.520
Go find Wai now.

1208
01:06:56.040 --> 01:06:57.480
He's on his way.

1209
01:06:58.240 --> 01:06:59.240
Calling the cops?

1210
01:06:59.800 --> 01:07:01.040
I'll beat them all too.

1211
01:07:02.520 --> 01:07:05.080
- Have you ever been in a fight?
- Never. I was a model student.

1212
01:07:16.240 --> 01:07:17.320
Get them!

1213
01:07:55.280 --> 01:07:57.440
Hey. Wai? What's taking you so long?

1214
01:07:57.520 --> 01:07:59.720
Your friend's fighting
with a whole damn army.

1215
01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:02.160
No. I mean he's being beaten up
by a whole damn army.

1216
01:10:14.720 --> 01:10:15.840
Don't hit me!

1217
01:10:15.920 --> 01:10:16.680
Mr. Fok?

1218
01:10:16.760 --> 01:10:18.240
Mr. Fok. it's me.

1219
01:10:18.320 --> 01:10:19.400
It's me.

1220
01:10:20.720 --> 01:10:22.400
You're lucky to be alive.

1221
01:10:24.600 --> 01:10:26.520
- I'll buy you dinner.
- Turns out Lau Siu-keung

1222
01:10:26.600 --> 01:10:28.760
is Chan Kwok-wing's half-brother.

1223
01:10:29.520 --> 01:10:30.720
I recorded everything.

1224
01:10:30.800 --> 01:10:33.000
This place belongs to Lau Siu-keung.

1225
01:10:33.080 --> 01:10:35.720
The guys in suits who attacked you earlier
are the security guards.

1226
01:10:35.800 --> 01:10:38.160
Every one of them
insisted on hiring a lawyer

1227
01:10:38.240 --> 01:10:40.680
and specifically asked
for Au Pak-man's law firm.

1228
01:10:40.760 --> 01:10:43.480
Justice will prevail.
Heaven is on our side.

1229
01:10:44.080 --> 01:10:46.160
The brothers are obstructing justice.

1230
01:10:46.240 --> 01:10:48.040
Ma Ka Kit's case has a good chance now.

1231
01:10:52.560 --> 01:10:53.560
Mr. Yeung.

1232
01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:55.200
Hey. Mr. Bao.

1233
01:10:55.280 --> 01:10:56.720
Got a second to talk?

1234
01:10:56.800 --> 01:10:58.520
I'm rushing to the High Court.

1235
01:10:58.600 --> 01:11:00.320
- What's the matter?
- It's urgent.

1236
01:11:00.400 --> 01:11:01.920
AU PAK-MAN. 42

1237
01:11:03.720 --> 01:11:05.320
How do you know Li Sze-man?

1238
01:11:05.400 --> 01:11:07.920
I was introduced by the owner
of the restaurant where Kit works.

1239
01:11:08.160 --> 01:11:10.080
<i>I think his last name is Lau.</i>

1240
01:11:10.160 --> 01:11:13.400
Uncle Ma said that Lau Siu-keung
introduced Au Pak-man to him.

1241
01:11:13.480 --> 01:11:15.320
Turns out Lau Siu-keung
and Chan Kwok-wing

1242
01:11:15.400 --> 01:11:16.720
are half-brothers.

1243
01:11:16.800 --> 01:11:18.800
They have long colluded
to obstruct justice.

1244
01:11:19.760 --> 01:11:21.280
Bao. why are you so enthusiastic?

1245
01:11:21.360 --> 01:11:22.440
<i>You even joined their team.</i>

1246
01:11:31.760 --> 01:11:34.920
<i>Uncle Ma is now filing
an official statement.</i>

1247
01:11:35.000 --> 01:11:37.200
You should go and take a look.
The evidence is real.

1248
01:11:37.280 --> 01:11:39.440
Now. the Legal Aid Department

1249
01:11:39.520 --> 01:11:42.320
is citing. "Judge misdirected the jury."

1250
01:11:42.400 --> 01:11:45.880
It has been remitted for retrial.
scheduled in 28 days.

1251
01:11:45.960 --> 01:11:47.200
I really don't understand.

1252
01:11:47.280 --> 01:11:50.400
Why are they retrying
such a small case over and over?

1253
01:11:50.480 --> 01:11:54.680
I don't want people to think
that the DOJ is unprofessional.

1254
01:11:54.760 --> 01:11:56.840
Once the statement is done.

1255
01:11:56.920 --> 01:11:59.160
the police will submit
the documents to the DOJ.

1256
01:11:59.240 --> 01:12:01.640
The DOJ will then consider
whether to accept it or not.

1257
01:12:01.720 --> 01:12:03.320
Of course I know.

1258
01:12:03.400 --> 01:12:05.120
But I'm done
with all the doubts between us.

1259
01:12:06.040 --> 01:12:07.680
What do you want to say? Spit it out.

1260
01:12:07.760 --> 01:12:10.720
The DOJ has prosecuted
Au Pak-man three times.

1261
01:12:10.800 --> 01:12:12.360
but he walked free every time.

1262
01:12:12.440 --> 01:12:15.040
It was the same prosecutor
all three times.

1263
01:12:15.120 --> 01:12:16.216
CHIEF PROSECUTOR: YEUNG DIT-LAP

1264
01:12:16.240 --> 01:12:17.600
You were the lead prosecutor.

1265
01:12:19.040 --> 01:12:20.920
- How long have you known me?
- Thirty-six years.

1266
01:12:21.000 --> 01:12:24.600
Don't you know I deal with thousands
of cases each year? Three cases?

1267
01:12:24.680 --> 01:12:26.040
Are you using this to question me?

1268
01:12:26.120 --> 01:12:28.480
- Mr Yeung.
- Accusing me over these three cases?

1269
01:12:29.160 --> 01:12:32.840
Just this afternoon.
I have 38 cases waiting for me.

1270
01:12:32.920 --> 01:12:35.000
If you have evidence
to support your accusations.

1271
01:12:35.080 --> 01:12:36.840
then please report me immediately.

1272
01:12:36.920 --> 01:12:39.840
Otherwise. don't waste my time
with this nonsense.

1273
01:12:43.920 --> 01:12:45.000
PAK-MAN DECLINED CALLS

1274
01:12:53.400 --> 01:12:54.320
I want a lawyer.

1275
01:12:54.400 --> 01:12:55.920
No matter how many retrials.

1276
01:12:56.000 --> 01:12:57.720
the result will be the same.
We won't lose.

1277
01:12:57.800 --> 01:12:59.440
I don't care about winning or losing.

1278
01:13:00.040 --> 01:13:01.856
What matters
is maintaining the public's trust.

1279
01:13:01.880 --> 01:13:04.840
Knowing that we have the ability
to uphold the rule of law.

1280
01:13:04.920 --> 01:13:07.536
Legal Aid has arranged for you to give
a statement at the police station.

1281
01:13:07.560 --> 01:13:09.200
As long as you expose Lau Siu-keung.

1282
01:13:09.280 --> 01:13:12.560
tell them he referred you to the lawyer.
then he's guilty of obstructing justice.

1283
01:13:12.640 --> 01:13:14.120
There will be a hope for Kit.

1284
01:13:15.720 --> 01:13:17.760
It seems Kit really has a chance.

1285
01:13:17.840 --> 01:13:18.720
Thank you.

1286
01:13:18.800 --> 01:13:20.360
Not at all. It's my duty.

1287
01:13:21.480 --> 01:13:23.120
But you will have to testify in court.

1288
01:13:23.200 --> 01:13:25.880
- Stay strong.
- Of course I will.

1289
01:13:25.960 --> 01:13:27.920
I hope that after Kit is released.

1290
01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:29.680
he can reform and return to his studies.

1291
01:13:29.760 --> 01:13:31.680
To grow into someone like you.
a great lawyer.

1292
01:13:31.760 --> 01:13:33.160
You're too kind.

1293
01:13:33.800 --> 01:13:36.600
Your grandson truly has artistic talent.

1294
01:13:36.680 --> 01:13:38.160
- I know. right?
- He draws very well.

1295
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:40.800
Nowadays. paintings are pricey.

1296
01:13:40.880 --> 01:13:42.560
Actually.

1297
01:13:42.640 --> 01:13:44.520
it doesn't matter what he studies.

1298
01:13:44.600 --> 01:13:47.000
What matters most is getting a girlfriend.

1299
01:13:47.080 --> 01:13:48.680
Seeing him build a family of his own.

1300
01:13:48.760 --> 01:13:50.360
That's all I hope for.

1301
01:13:50.440 --> 01:13:51.720
I look forward to his wedding.

1302
01:13:51.800 --> 01:13:53.040
Of course I'll invite you.

1303
01:13:54.280 --> 01:13:55.320
Let me use the restroom.

1304
01:13:56.040 --> 01:13:57.320
You can sit at the host's table.

1305
01:13:57.400 --> 01:13:59.000
As long as I get to eat.

1306
01:15:04.520 --> 01:15:06.720
I beg you. Prosecutor Fok.

1307
01:15:07.360 --> 01:15:09.080
You work for the DOJ. right?

1308
01:15:09.160 --> 01:15:10.920
Can you talk to the judge

1309
01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:13.320
to release me for one day? Just one day.

1310
01:15:13.920 --> 01:15:15.960
After that. even a lifetime
in jail wouldn't matter.

1311
01:15:18.320 --> 01:15:19.560
I want revenge.

1312
01:15:28.800 --> 01:15:29.960
I don't understand.

1313
01:15:31.160 --> 01:15:32.520
I really…

1314
01:15:32.600 --> 01:15:35.000
I don't understand.
Why won't anyone help me?

1315
01:15:36.280 --> 01:15:38.320
I really didn't do anything.

1316
01:15:39.080 --> 01:15:40.520
I lent my address

1317
01:15:40.600 --> 01:15:43.920
just to make a few thousand
to help my grandpa with living expenses.

1318
01:15:44.600 --> 01:15:47.120
I simply wished
that we could have better meals.

1319
01:15:47.200 --> 01:15:49.320
eat together at a nice table.

1320
01:15:49.400 --> 01:15:52.360
and have a home that doesn't leak.
That's it.

1321
01:15:53.000 --> 01:15:54.640
Did I really do something wrong?

1322
01:16:08.240 --> 01:16:09.616
<i>Ma Ka-kit's relative recently died…</i>

1323
01:16:09.640 --> 01:16:10.896
<i>- Now. people are very worried…
- Is it related to the case…</i>

1324
01:16:10.920 --> 01:16:12.256
<i>Everyone is paying
close attention to this case.</i>

1325
01:16:12.280 --> 01:16:13.120
<i>Is someone trying to silence a witness?</i>

1326
01:16:13.200 --> 01:16:14.936
<i>Did the Department of Justice
accuse the wrong person?</i>

1327
01:16:14.960 --> 01:16:15.880
<i>Everyone is paying
close attention to this case.</i>

1328
01:16:15.960 --> 01:16:17.800
<i>How do you feel about handling this case?</i>

1329
01:16:17.880 --> 01:16:20.000
This case has entered
the judicial process.

1330
01:16:20.080 --> 01:16:22.600
I should not comment here. Sorry.

1331
01:16:22.680 --> 01:16:25.600
If the appeal is successful. would it
damage the reputation of the DOJ?

1332
01:16:25.680 --> 01:16:29.320
The DOJ's image
doesn't matter to the rest of the world.

1333
01:16:29.400 --> 01:16:31.280
The DOJ works based on evidence.

1334
01:16:31.360 --> 01:16:33.840
<i>We present the evidence to the court.</i>

1335
01:16:33.920 --> 01:16:35.960
<i>The court makes the final decision.</i>

1336
01:16:42.080 --> 01:16:42.960
Here.

1337
01:16:43.040 --> 01:16:44.040
Okay.

1338
01:16:45.560 --> 01:16:46.840
- Check again.
- Okay.

1339
01:16:52.920 --> 01:16:54.560
We've checked this matter many times.

1340
01:16:55.160 --> 01:16:56.160
No leads.

1341
01:16:56.840 --> 01:16:59.120
No witnesses. no fingerprints.
no murder weapon.

1342
01:17:00.120 --> 01:17:01.440
Lots of stores across the street.

1343
01:17:01.520 --> 01:17:04.520
Have you checked their CCTV?

1344
01:17:05.640 --> 01:17:09.240
Have you checked for any
nearby cars and pedestrians?

1345
01:17:14.000 --> 01:17:16.880
Not finding anything
means you haven't done your best.

1346
01:17:21.040 --> 01:17:24.240
All of us have been grinding
for 48 hours straight.

1347
01:17:24.320 --> 01:17:25.680
You believe we don't want to help?

1348
01:17:25.720 --> 01:17:27.720
No evidence and no witnesses.

1349
01:17:27.800 --> 01:17:29.000
What can we do?

1350
01:17:29.080 --> 01:17:31.080
If there's no way. then find one.

1351
01:17:31.160 --> 01:17:32.800
I trust you.

1352
01:17:32.880 --> 01:17:35.080
but you need to trust yourself too.

1353
01:17:35.680 --> 01:17:37.760
Do you remember what we used to say?

1354
01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:41.520
- Stick to our post...
- Stick to our post?

1355
01:17:41.600 --> 01:17:43.720
Everyone here
is staying firm at their post!

1356
01:17:45.800 --> 01:17:47.720
But we still couldn't solve it.

1357
01:17:49.960 --> 01:17:51.840
Even the police are helpless sometimes.

1358
01:17:52.960 --> 01:17:54.880
It's not like we can investigate
however we want.

1359
01:17:55.560 --> 01:17:57.040
Now I understand

1360
01:17:57.120 --> 01:17:58.560
why you gave up back then.

1361
01:18:13.000 --> 01:18:14.000
Mr. Fok.

1362
01:18:15.280 --> 01:18:17.040
Hi. madam. Long time no see.

1363
01:18:18.160 --> 01:18:19.160
Is this your son?

1364
01:18:19.800 --> 01:18:20.680
Yes.

1365
01:18:20.760 --> 01:18:22.240
- His name is Luke.
- Hello. Uncle.

1366
01:18:22.320 --> 01:18:23.600
Hello. Luke.

1367
01:18:24.440 --> 01:18:25.920
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

1368
01:18:27.080 --> 01:18:28.200
Still in the Emergency Unit?

1369
01:18:28.280 --> 01:18:30.760
Yes. I just finished my board interview.

1370
01:18:30.840 --> 01:18:32.160
There's a chance for a promotion.

1371
01:18:32.200 --> 01:18:33.120
Great. Keep it up.

1372
01:18:33.200 --> 01:18:36.080
- Stick to your post and fight crime.
- Stick to your post and fight crime.

1373
01:18:36.680 --> 01:18:37.840
<i>Officer Fok.</i>

1374
01:18:37.920 --> 01:18:39.520
<i>Actually. I was three months pregnant</i>

1375
01:18:39.600 --> 01:18:41.920
<i>during that operation seven years ago.</i>

1376
01:18:42.000 --> 01:18:44.000
<i>If you didn't save me.</i>

1377
01:18:44.080 --> 01:18:45.480
<i>he wouldn't be sitting here.</i>

1378
01:18:46.080 --> 01:18:47.080
<i>Thank you.</i>

1379
01:18:49.080 --> 01:18:50.600
<i>I never gave up.</i>

1380
01:18:51.280 --> 01:18:52.760
I'm just getting old.

1381
01:18:53.280 --> 01:18:55.080
I can't be on the front line

1382
01:18:55.160 --> 01:18:58.080
my whole life. so I really need your help.

1383
01:19:00.920 --> 01:19:01.960
That's why

1384
01:19:02.680 --> 01:19:04.880
I transferred
to the Department of Justice.

1385
01:19:06.760 --> 01:19:08.440
To defend the last line
of the rule of law.

1386
01:19:21.320 --> 01:19:22.720
As long as you have faith.

1387
01:19:24.560 --> 01:19:25.560
you can do it.

1388
01:19:27.600 --> 01:19:29.040
Stay true to your mission.

1389
01:19:30.520 --> 01:19:32.720
It would be great
if everyone had your enthusiasm.

1390
01:19:32.800 --> 01:19:33.800
You have it too.

1391
01:19:35.840 --> 01:19:36.840
Understand.

1392
01:19:44.000 --> 01:19:45.800
Alright. Let's keep going.

1393
01:19:47.600 --> 01:19:49.200
Keep going. everyone!

1394
01:19:49.280 --> 01:19:50.280
Copy that.

1395
01:20:13.240 --> 01:20:14.480
Gotta go.

1396
01:20:15.920 --> 01:20:16.960
Bao Ding.

1397
01:20:17.040 --> 01:20:18.600
Work's over. You're not leaving?

1398
01:20:18.680 --> 01:20:20.760
If you're not with us. then go.

1399
01:20:24.200 --> 01:20:25.200
Hey.

1400
01:20:26.280 --> 01:20:29.200
There are still over a dozen cases.
We can't finish them before the trial.

1401
01:20:32.800 --> 01:20:34.400
You should have stayed a police officer.

1402
01:20:34.440 --> 01:20:36.520
If I hadn't met you.
I wouldn't have to work so hard.

1403
01:20:37.440 --> 01:20:40.080
Why the sudden transfer to the DOJ?

1404
01:20:40.160 --> 01:20:41.760
I have no idea why you did this.

1405
01:20:43.680 --> 01:20:45.320
Do you want to know why?

1406
01:20:46.600 --> 01:20:48.800
Tell me. Stop being mysterious.

1407
01:20:55.640 --> 01:20:58.920
Because I think our work

1408
01:20:59.000 --> 01:21:01.400
is a beacon that never fades.

1409
01:21:02.280 --> 01:21:05.120
It shines the glory
of fairness and justice

1410
01:21:05.680 --> 01:21:10.800
into the hearts of the people.
into every dark corner.

1411
01:21:14.600 --> 01:21:16.800
I'm getting old.
I can't catch thieves anymore.

1412
01:21:16.880 --> 01:21:18.240
My knees aren't working well.

1413
01:21:19.200 --> 01:21:21.200
That's not my issue. I'm still young.

1414
01:21:30.160 --> 01:21:31.160
You are right.

1415
01:21:31.680 --> 01:21:33.056
Remember your first case. the bet we made?

1416
01:21:33.080 --> 01:21:35.720
There was a third person at the scene.
It's a conspiracy to murder.

1417
01:21:35.920 --> 01:21:37.200
A bet's a bet.

1418
01:21:47.800 --> 01:21:49.560
I'm good at reviewing documents.
Let me help.

1419
01:21:51.200 --> 01:21:53.560
There are lots of documents.
Let's go through them together.

1420
01:21:54.520 --> 01:21:56.000
I'll take care of this box.

1421
01:22:06.960 --> 01:22:08.640
The beacon…

1422
01:22:10.800 --> 01:22:12.000
I've extinguished it.

1423
01:22:25.720 --> 01:22:26.720
- Fok Sir.
- Okay.

1424
01:22:29.040 --> 01:22:30.760
The criminal organization has a pattern.

1425
01:22:30.840 --> 01:22:32.560
There are more victims like Ma Ka-kit.

1426
01:22:32.640 --> 01:22:34.200
There are many Ma Ka-kits out there.

1427
01:22:34.280 --> 01:22:35.600
<i>Before the trial.</i>

1428
01:22:35.680 --> 01:22:36.976
<i>we need to find one more Ma Ka-kit</i>

1429
01:22:37.000 --> 01:22:38.336
- <i>who is willing to testify.</i>
- Police.

1430
01:22:38.360 --> 01:22:40.320
But importing drugs
into Hong Kong by mail…

1431
01:22:40.400 --> 01:22:41.616
<i>There are over 300 similar cases per year.</i>

1432
01:22:41.640 --> 01:22:43.520
<i>Maybe over 1.000 cases in total.</i>

1433
01:22:43.600 --> 01:22:44.936
- We only have a few days.
- I know it's difficult.

1434
01:22:44.960 --> 01:22:46.640
but I know you can do it.

1435
01:23:04.720 --> 01:23:07.256
<i>A young man went through what you did.
You could help him by appearing in court.</i>

1436
01:23:07.280 --> 01:23:09.160
I've done my sentence already.
What do you want?

1437
01:23:09.200 --> 01:23:10.480
Go away.

1438
01:23:14.720 --> 01:23:16.720
My son just got out
from the juvenile home.

1439
01:23:16.800 --> 01:23:17.800
Leave him alone.

1440
01:23:33.360 --> 01:23:35.480
<i>I don't mind giving a statement
at the police station.</i>

1441
01:23:35.560 --> 01:23:37.400
I'd rather not go to court. though.

1442
01:23:37.480 --> 01:23:39.336
I don't want others to know
I've been to prison.

1443
01:23:39.360 --> 01:23:41.640
I understand.
but there's a young man just like you.

1444
01:23:41.720 --> 01:23:44.160
He also received a parcel
and was accused of drug trafficking.

1445
01:23:46.520 --> 01:23:47.760
Stop bothering me.

1446
01:23:55.360 --> 01:23:57.336
Was it this person
who introduced you to the lawyer?

1447
01:23:57.360 --> 01:23:59.280
He has harmed many people
with the same method.

1448
01:24:01.680 --> 01:24:02.760
Please help.

1449
01:24:02.840 --> 01:24:06.280
A young man also received a package
and was accused of drug trafficking.

1450
01:24:07.720 --> 01:24:09.640
If you testify in court. you can save him.

1451
01:24:15.400 --> 01:24:17.240
Everyone. Bingo.

1452
01:24:17.320 --> 01:24:18.160
Someone agreed to appear in court.

1453
01:24:18.240 --> 01:24:19.400
Well done!

1454
01:24:23.800 --> 01:24:25.080
Thank you!

1455
01:24:25.160 --> 01:24:26.560
Well done!

1456
01:24:32.640 --> 01:24:33.840
Well done!

1457
01:24:35.080 --> 01:24:36.560
Well done. Mr. Fok.

1458
01:24:41.680 --> 01:24:42.840
Hello. Mr. Fok.

1459
01:24:42.920 --> 01:24:45.280
You took leave today. so I came over
to check on you.

1460
01:24:45.880 --> 01:24:47.120
Is everything alright?

1461
01:24:48.800 --> 01:24:49.800
Thank you.

1462
01:24:53.280 --> 01:24:55.480
How are things now?

1463
01:24:56.680 --> 01:24:59.720
I never thought
the case would get this serious.

1464
01:24:59.800 --> 01:25:00.800
Someone even got killed.

1465
01:25:01.680 --> 01:25:03.840
When will you be done with this?

1466
01:25:03.920 --> 01:25:05.320
Uncle Ma has been killed.

1467
01:25:06.800 --> 01:25:08.160
Are you pretending not to know?

1468
01:25:08.240 --> 01:25:10.240
His death is a separate case.

1469
01:25:10.320 --> 01:25:11.480
A criminal case.

1470
01:25:11.560 --> 01:25:13.320
We are the Department of Justice.

1471
01:25:16.080 --> 01:25:18.200
Ever thought of becoming a cop again?

1472
01:25:18.280 --> 01:25:20.640
Then you can investigate cases
and catch criminals.

1473
01:25:20.720 --> 01:25:22.320
You can even become a defense lawyer.

1474
01:25:22.400 --> 01:25:24.160
After all. you enjoy being
a defense lawyer.

1475
01:25:24.680 --> 01:25:26.440
You're wasting your talents at the DOJ.

1476
01:25:26.520 --> 01:25:28.280
Do you know what the DOJ is for?

1477
01:25:28.360 --> 01:25:29.720
Let me tell you.

1478
01:25:29.800 --> 01:25:31.640
The DOJ is the final gate
of the rule of law.

1479
01:25:31.720 --> 01:25:33.080
Now. Uncle Ma

1480
01:25:34.400 --> 01:25:35.400
has been murdered.

1481
01:25:35.480 --> 01:25:37.056
Ma Ka-kit will be imprisoned for 27 years.

1482
01:25:37.080 --> 01:25:39.216
Even if he's guilty.
is 27 years a reasonable sentence?

1483
01:25:39.240 --> 01:25:40.440
You tell me.

1484
01:25:42.760 --> 01:25:43.680
Honestly.

1485
01:25:43.760 --> 01:25:44.880
27 years is a bit excessive.

1486
01:25:45.960 --> 01:25:47.000
But we are the DOJ.

1487
01:25:47.080 --> 01:25:50.000
Do you know how many
pending cases we have?

1488
01:25:50.080 --> 01:25:52.880
If every colleague works the way you do.

1489
01:25:52.960 --> 01:25:54.640
the DOJ would be paralyzed. Understand?

1490
01:25:54.720 --> 01:25:56.600
Given your current state of mind.

1491
01:25:56.680 --> 01:25:59.256
you are no longer suitable to be
the lead prosecutor of this case.

1492
01:25:59.280 --> 01:26:01.840
It's even more unsuitable
for you to remain in the DOJ.

1493
01:26:01.920 --> 01:26:03.400
I have submitted a letter to the CSB

1494
01:26:03.480 --> 01:26:05.320
requesting your transfer.

1495
01:26:05.400 --> 01:26:07.240
You will receive notice
in one month. okay?

1496
01:26:07.960 --> 01:26:08.800
Are you serious?

1497
01:26:08.880 --> 01:26:09.880
- Yeah.
- Get out.

1498
01:26:09.960 --> 01:26:11.120
Thank you.

1499
01:26:14.760 --> 01:26:16.680
You're a loser.

1500
01:26:17.440 --> 01:26:18.720
Cut the act.

1501
01:26:18.800 --> 01:26:20.920
- All that education. you're still a loser.
- What?

1502
01:26:21.000 --> 01:26:22.256
Wearing a suit doesn't make you classy.

1503
01:26:22.280 --> 01:26:23.200
You're the type

1504
01:26:23.280 --> 01:26:25.680
who'd just walk past an old lady
falling in the street.

1505
01:26:25.760 --> 01:26:29.360
You have no friends. You're selfish.
You only think of yourself.

1506
01:26:29.440 --> 01:26:32.160
You don't even own a pet.
Go home and jerk off.

1507
01:26:32.240 --> 01:26:33.800
Oh. don't leave just yet.

1508
01:26:38.680 --> 01:26:40.696
Here's the evidence
of your collaboration with Au Pak-man.

1509
01:26:40.720 --> 01:26:42.400
Stop slandering me!

1510
01:26:43.040 --> 01:26:45.296
- What's wrong with you?
- Why are you taking off your jacket?

1511
01:26:45.320 --> 01:26:47.296
- You want a one-on-one?
- I've put up with you too long.

1512
01:26:47.320 --> 01:26:48.656
- Come on!
- Talking about Au Pak-man all the time.

1513
01:26:48.680 --> 01:26:50.600
The Treasury pays you
thousands each month.

1514
01:26:50.680 --> 01:26:52.560
- You bastard.
- I'm giving you one chance.

1515
01:26:52.640 --> 01:26:53.696
- Yeung Dit-lap.
- If you win.

1516
01:26:53.720 --> 01:26:55.336
- Let's see how strong you are.
- I'll let you off.

1517
01:26:55.360 --> 01:26:56.656
- Let's see what you've got.
- Let's fight!

1518
01:26:56.680 --> 01:26:57.880
Come on!

1519
01:26:57.960 --> 01:26:59.096
- Fight with me?
- The world is full of people

1520
01:26:59.120 --> 01:27:00.120
- like Au.
- Cut the crap.

1521
01:27:00.160 --> 01:27:01.160
Can you arrest them all?

1522
01:27:01.200 --> 01:27:02.240
Damn you.

1523
01:27:03.000 --> 01:27:04.320
Come on.

1524
01:27:05.800 --> 01:27:06.800
Let's go.

1525
01:27:13.600 --> 01:27:16.120
Beat me and I'll back you up.

1526
01:27:19.240 --> 01:27:20.480
Get ready to back me up. then.

1527
01:27:20.560 --> 01:27:21.560
Damn. You wish.

1528
01:27:31.000 --> 01:27:32.456
So. you're playing tricks on me
with blank papers?

1529
01:27:32.480 --> 01:27:34.440
This is the only way to ignite
your determination.

1530
01:27:35.720 --> 01:27:36.800
You have to keep your word.

1531
01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:51.640
Brother Tung.
here are the US dollars you asked for.

1532
01:27:51.720 --> 01:27:52.880
Count it yourself.

1533
01:27:54.160 --> 01:27:56.760
Nakamura. put that over there.

1534
01:27:56.840 --> 01:27:57.840
Yes. sir.

1535
01:28:00.560 --> 01:28:04.640
Gentlemen. the money laundry is done.

1536
01:28:04.720 --> 01:28:06.600
If you need anything. call me anytime.

1537
01:28:09.640 --> 01:28:10.840
Smart guy.

1538
01:28:14.800 --> 01:28:16.840
Man delivered the goods as agreed.

1539
01:28:16.920 --> 01:28:18.360
Everybody's happy.

1540
01:28:18.440 --> 01:28:21.880
But I still have something
to ask Lau Siu-keung.

1541
01:28:21.960 --> 01:28:23.400
- Hey.
- Yes. Tung?

1542
01:28:23.480 --> 01:28:25.480
The police are looking
for evidence against you.

1543
01:28:26.160 --> 01:28:27.440
This definitely affects Man too.

1544
01:28:27.520 --> 01:28:28.720
You'll bring trouble to us.

1545
01:28:28.800 --> 01:28:30.840
It's my fault. I'll settle the matter.

1546
01:28:30.920 --> 01:28:34.000
Let's not bring up anything
that ruins the vibe.

1547
01:28:34.080 --> 01:28:35.480
We're all so happy now.

1548
01:28:35.560 --> 01:28:36.600
Let's just drink.

1549
01:28:37.440 --> 01:28:39.160
I've sorted it out with Keung already.

1550
01:28:39.240 --> 01:28:41.640
He will turn himself in and plead guilty.

1551
01:28:41.720 --> 01:28:44.480
Then the whole matter will be resolved.

1552
01:28:44.560 --> 01:28:46.520
In any case. it won't bother you.

1553
01:28:46.600 --> 01:28:48.680
Come on. Let's drink.

1554
01:28:51.120 --> 01:28:52.120
Here.

1555
01:28:52.160 --> 01:28:53.360
Thank you. Sang.

1556
01:28:54.400 --> 01:28:55.240
Gentlemen…

1557
01:28:55.320 --> 01:28:56.680
Keung is very capable.

1558
01:28:56.760 --> 01:28:59.680
If there's any offense.
please forgive him.

1559
01:28:59.760 --> 01:29:02.680
For my sake. don't blame him.

1560
01:29:02.760 --> 01:29:04.080
Today

1561
01:29:04.600 --> 01:29:05.880
is Sang's birthday.

1562
01:29:06.640 --> 01:29:08.440
I prepared
a small birthday present for you.

1563
01:29:11.360 --> 01:29:12.680
See if you like it.

1564
01:29:21.000 --> 01:29:22.000
Man…

1565
01:29:22.840 --> 01:29:25.160
- Such a smart guy.
- Sang…

1566
01:29:25.240 --> 01:29:26.760
I wish you dazzling charm.

1567
01:29:26.840 --> 01:29:29.240
Like fireworks. Charming forever.

1568
01:29:29.320 --> 01:29:30.360
Time's up.

1569
01:29:38.760 --> 01:29:39.880
Have you gone crazy?

1570
01:29:40.400 --> 01:29:42.280
Today is my birthday.

1571
01:29:42.360 --> 01:29:43.560
We agreed I would shoot.

1572
01:29:43.640 --> 01:29:45.440
Yes. it's your birthday.

1573
01:29:45.520 --> 01:29:47.400
but we agreed to shoot at 12:30.

1574
01:29:47.480 --> 01:29:50.640
- You shot the old guy. It's my turn now.
- If you wanted to shoot.

1575
01:29:50.720 --> 01:29:52.640
you should have done it
at the stern of the ship.

1576
01:29:52.720 --> 01:29:55.320
You made a mess.

1577
01:29:55.400 --> 01:29:58.360
Now I need to replace the furniture.
It takes time to order it from Italy.

1578
01:29:58.440 --> 01:30:00.960
I couldn't wait.
What if he drank all my booze?

1579
01:30:02.160 --> 01:30:03.440
Let's drink.

1580
01:30:04.840 --> 01:30:06.040
Happy Birthday.

1581
01:30:15.040 --> 01:30:17.096
The body in the sea this morning
has been confirmed as Lau Siu-keung.

1582
01:30:17.120 --> 01:30:18.976
Even with the testimony
from the laundry shop girl.

1583
01:30:19.000 --> 01:30:20.576
we still lack of evidence to charge him.

1584
01:30:20.600 --> 01:30:22.176
Their next target will be Chan Kwok-wing.

1585
01:30:22.200 --> 01:30:24.520
We don't know if he's hiding
or has already been killed.

1586
01:30:24.600 --> 01:30:25.800
We can't find him.

1587
01:30:25.880 --> 01:30:26.760
The trial is about to begin.

1588
01:30:26.840 --> 01:30:28.360
We need to find Chan Kwok-wing ASAP.

1589
01:31:11.320 --> 01:31:13.800
As long as you tell the truth.

1590
01:31:13.880 --> 01:31:15.600
we will help you shorten your sentence.

1591
01:31:16.280 --> 01:31:18.000
And if your testimony can help

1592
01:31:18.080 --> 01:31:20.600
incriminate the whole gang
of drug traffickers.

1593
01:31:20.680 --> 01:31:23.520
I will also consider helping you
apply for amnesty.

1594
01:31:23.600 --> 01:31:26.520
Being a tainted witness
is in your best interest.

1595
01:31:26.600 --> 01:31:29.120
Your sentence reduction
depends on how much you say.

1596
01:31:31.880 --> 01:31:33.480
I have evidence about Lau Siu-keung

1597
01:31:34.000 --> 01:31:36.080
that can prove
that Au Pak-man is the culprit.

1598
01:31:36.160 --> 01:31:37.760
I even know where his drug den is.

1599
01:31:37.840 --> 01:31:39.760
I want a shortened sentence.

1600
01:31:39.840 --> 01:31:41.560
Do you have any other choices?

1601
01:32:04.960 --> 01:32:05.960
Prosecutor Yeung.

1602
01:32:06.480 --> 01:32:07.560
Fok Chi-ho isn't here.

1603
01:32:07.640 --> 01:32:09.800
Just do what I say later.

1604
01:32:30.320 --> 01:32:31.320
My leg…

1605
01:32:32.120 --> 01:32:33.440
I can't walk.

1606
01:32:33.520 --> 01:32:34.520
Help me.

1607
01:32:35.080 --> 01:32:37.080
- Sit down.
- Help me.

1608
01:32:37.160 --> 01:32:39.160
- Can you still walk?
- Take him with you.

1609
01:32:39.240 --> 01:32:40.800
Court is in session. Get going.

1610
01:32:40.880 --> 01:32:41.920
- Go.
- Enough? Sir?

1611
01:32:42.000 --> 01:32:43.560
Help me. Officer.

1612
01:32:43.640 --> 01:32:44.696
- Take care.
- Call the police.

1613
01:32:44.720 --> 01:32:46.160
Just call the cops.

1614
01:32:46.240 --> 01:32:47.440
Don't let me die.

1615
01:32:49.000 --> 01:32:50.800
Quickly. call the cops.

1616
01:32:52.360 --> 01:32:54.000
I'm Inspector Lee King-wai.

1617
01:32:54.080 --> 01:32:55.880
I'm at the intersection of Ki Lung Street…

1618
01:33:01.880 --> 01:33:02.880
Hey.

1619
01:33:03.560 --> 01:33:04.800
Help me.

1620
01:33:06.440 --> 01:33:08.200
Don't let me die.

1621
01:33:08.280 --> 01:33:10.000
Hey. Help me.

1622
01:33:14.160 --> 01:33:15.960
Defendant Ma Ka-kit's appeal

1623
01:33:16.040 --> 01:33:18.560
in the drug trafficking
conspiracy case was successful.

1624
01:33:18.640 --> 01:33:20.640
The case will be retried today.

1625
01:33:20.720 --> 01:33:21.920
Miss Cheung Yeuk-sum.

1626
01:33:22.000 --> 01:33:25.920
A few years ago.
you received a parcel at your home.

1627
01:33:26.000 --> 01:33:28.760
Inside. there were 500 grams of cocaine.

1628
01:33:28.840 --> 01:33:32.160
and at that time.
you admitted to drug trafficking.

1629
01:33:32.240 --> 01:33:33.440
Is that true?

1630
01:33:33.520 --> 01:33:34.800
Actually. it was Chan Kwok-wing.

1631
01:33:34.840 --> 01:33:36.520
<i>He gave me HK$1000 to use my home address.</i>

1632
01:33:36.560 --> 01:33:39.280
<i>I didn't know there were drugs
in that parcel.</i>

1633
01:33:39.360 --> 01:33:43.680
My former boss. Lau Siu-keung.
introduced me to Au Pak-man.

1634
01:33:43.760 --> 01:33:46.440
They were the ones
who told me to plead guilty.

1635
01:33:46.520 --> 01:33:47.400
Do you have evidence?

1636
01:33:47.480 --> 01:33:49.360
I've been jailed for this.
That's evidence!

1637
01:33:49.440 --> 01:33:53.720
The key figures in our case.
Chan Kwok-wing and Lau Siu-keung.

1638
01:33:53.800 --> 01:33:55.760
are not present in the courtroom.

1639
01:33:56.280 --> 01:33:58.760
So. I would like to summon
the next witness.

1640
01:33:58.840 --> 01:34:00.440
Mr. Au Pak-man. to testify

1641
01:34:01.120 --> 01:34:04.880
and help reconstruct
the sequence of events.

1642
01:34:07.240 --> 01:34:10.240
<i>This case was actually easy for me
to handle within the law.</i>

1643
01:34:10.320 --> 01:34:11.536
<i>You bastards insisted on killing.</i>

1644
01:34:11.560 --> 01:34:13.656
<i>You killed the older one.
but let the little one walk.</i>

1645
01:34:13.680 --> 01:34:16.320
<i>If Chan Kwok-wing
has any evidence. I'm screwed.</i>

1646
01:34:16.400 --> 01:34:19.320
If you run away.
this case will never be closed.

1647
01:34:19.400 --> 01:34:21.600
Sooner or later. the police
will find out more and more.

1648
01:34:21.680 --> 01:34:23.080
Eventually. we'll both be doomed.

1649
01:34:23.160 --> 01:34:26.560
Settle it in court tomorrow.
and we'll all be happy.

1650
01:34:26.640 --> 01:34:28.120
Are you crazy?

1651
01:34:28.200 --> 01:34:29.720
Are you forcing me to appear in court?

1652
01:34:30.120 --> 01:34:31.560
You've got to be kidding me.

1653
01:34:31.640 --> 01:34:34.360
If I go down. you're going with me.

1654
01:34:34.440 --> 01:34:35.600
<i>Use your damn brain.</i>

1655
01:34:35.680 --> 01:34:36.976
<i>How much have you earned
over the years. thanks to me?</i>

1656
01:34:37.000 --> 01:34:38.760
<i>Without me. you're nothing but shit.</i>

1657
01:34:38.840 --> 01:34:41.800
I'm screwed. It's just a matter of time.

1658
01:34:42.880 --> 01:34:44.360
Stay calm.

1659
01:34:44.440 --> 01:34:46.840
<i>Let's fix this together.</i>

1660
01:34:46.920 --> 01:34:49.480
<i>I've arranged it all. Do you know?</i>

1661
01:34:50.160 --> 01:34:53.880
Where on Earth
does the sunrise appear first?

1662
01:34:55.960 --> 01:34:57.840
<i>It's Fiji.</i>

1663
01:34:58.440 --> 01:35:00.920
<i>I already bought a small island there.</i>

1664
01:35:01.000 --> 01:35:03.280
<i>I'm ready to go and enjoy my life.</i>

1665
01:35:03.360 --> 01:35:04.760
In Hong Kong.

1666
01:35:05.320 --> 01:35:06.840
there are skyscrapers everywhere.

1667
01:35:07.600 --> 01:35:10.120
It's hard to see the sunrise anymore.

1668
01:35:13.320 --> 01:35:14.600
In Chan Kwok-wing's testimony.

1669
01:35:14.680 --> 01:35:17.280
he also indicated

1670
01:35:17.360 --> 01:35:19.760
that he and his brother.
Lau Siu-keung. were working for you.

1671
01:35:20.600 --> 01:35:23.760
He was primarily responsible
for borrowing others' addresses

1672
01:35:23.840 --> 01:35:25.160
and receiving parcels.

1673
01:35:25.680 --> 01:35:27.776
His brother was responsible
for introducing lawyers to the victims.

1674
01:35:27.800 --> 01:35:32.040
including Miss Cheung Yeuk-sum
and Mr. Ma Ka-kit.

1675
01:35:32.120 --> 01:35:34.360
What's your explanation
for these accusations?

1676
01:35:34.880 --> 01:35:35.880
<i>Listen to me.</i>

1677
01:35:35.920 --> 01:35:39.320
<i>Go to court tomorrow
and resolve the matter.</i>

1678
01:35:39.400 --> 01:35:40.000
KUEN HANG CLUB

1679
01:35:40.080 --> 01:35:41.600
<i>I'll take you with me to Fiji.</i>

1680
01:35:41.680 --> 01:35:43.000
<i>Once we're there.</i>

1681
01:35:44.440 --> 01:35:47.280
<i>you'll be able to see
the sunrise every day.</i>

1682
01:35:47.880 --> 01:35:49.840
<i>I'll take care of things</i>

1683
01:35:49.920 --> 01:35:51.600
<i>outside of the courtroom.</i>

1684
01:35:53.280 --> 01:35:54.560
First of all.

1685
01:35:55.440 --> 01:35:58.080
I don't know what statement
he gave to the police.

1686
01:35:58.160 --> 01:35:59.760
But one thing I do know is that

1687
01:35:59.840 --> 01:36:02.000
his claims are meaningless.

1688
01:36:02.080 --> 01:36:04.080
unless he shows up in court to testify.

1689
01:36:05.080 --> 01:36:08.640
Prosecutor Yeung.
I know exactly what you're planning.

1690
01:36:08.720 --> 01:36:10.440
You're using my courtroom

1691
01:36:10.520 --> 01:36:12.440
to try and expose the crimes of others.

1692
01:36:12.520 --> 01:36:15.600
What are you trying to achieve in the end?

1693
01:36:15.680 --> 01:36:17.560
To answer your question. Your Honor.

1694
01:36:17.640 --> 01:36:18.880
I want to request

1695
01:36:18.960 --> 01:36:22.120
that Chan Kwok-wing testifies in court
as a special witness for the prosecution.

1696
01:36:22.200 --> 01:36:24.360
He didn't submit a request.

1697
01:36:25.160 --> 01:36:27.680
Without a request. I won't approve it.

1698
01:36:27.760 --> 01:36:30.280
- It is unfair to the defense.
- Your Honor.

1699
01:36:30.360 --> 01:36:31.920
I'm fine with it.

1700
01:36:35.080 --> 01:36:36.280
Are you two messing with me?

1701
01:36:36.360 --> 01:36:37.400
Your Honor.

1702
01:36:37.480 --> 01:36:40.840
I humbly request your approval
for Chan Kwok-wing to testify in court.

1703
01:36:40.920 --> 01:36:43.120
If you're not satisfied
after hearing his testimony.

1704
01:36:43.200 --> 01:36:45.680
I'm willing to bear
the consequences and responsibilities.

1705
01:36:45.760 --> 01:36:48.240
When will your witness appear. then?

1706
01:37:11.320 --> 01:37:17.600
<i>Please stand back from the train doors.</i>

1707
01:40:32.320 --> 01:40:33.960
Officer Fok.

1708
01:41:48.320 --> 01:41:49.560
Prosecutor Fok.

1709
01:41:51.720 --> 01:41:53.840
Sang and I spent ten years

1710
01:41:55.000 --> 01:41:57.560
hiding in Cambodia all because of you.

1711
01:41:58.360 --> 01:41:59.920
You've arrested so many people.

1712
01:42:00.000 --> 01:42:01.680
Of course. you can't recognize me.

1713
01:42:10.600 --> 01:42:12.360
That stubborn old man. Uncle Ma.

1714
01:42:12.440 --> 01:42:14.200
I stabbed him a dozen times.

1715
01:42:14.280 --> 01:42:16.360
His guts spilled all over the floor.

1716
01:42:16.440 --> 01:42:18.040
I really enjoyed it. It's your turn now.

1717
01:44:04.320 --> 01:44:07.160
This is how the law works. Prosecutor Fok.

1718
01:44:08.120 --> 01:44:09.320
Hey.

1719
01:44:11.760 --> 01:44:13.000
Objection.

1720
01:45:08.200 --> 01:45:09.560
Would you like to appeal?

1721
01:45:09.640 --> 01:45:11.440
The courtroom is a place
to uncover the truth.

1722
01:45:12.000 --> 01:45:14.680
Time means nothing
in the face of the truth.

1723
01:45:14.760 --> 01:45:16.840
So. no matter how much time it takes.

1724
01:45:16.920 --> 01:45:19.000
we must wait for the truth to come out.

1725
01:45:19.080 --> 01:45:20.360
Right?

1726
01:45:20.440 --> 01:45:23.040
Prosecutor Yeung. could you
please stop reciting poetry here?

1727
01:45:23.120 --> 01:45:25.120
When can he come?

1728
01:45:45.400 --> 01:45:47.240
Sorry. Your Honor…

1729
01:45:48.120 --> 01:45:49.240
There was some traffic.

1730
01:45:53.440 --> 01:45:55.160
<i>My brother left evidence for me.</i>

1731
01:45:55.240 --> 01:45:58.360
<i>It includes account books.
drug trade records. and…</i>

1732
01:45:59.160 --> 01:46:00.280
<i>Au Pak-man's bank accounts.</i>

1733
01:46:01.240 --> 01:46:03.320
He told me to disclose everything
to protect myself.

1734
01:46:04.040 --> 01:46:07.240
Ma Ka-kit didn't know
the parcel contained drugs.

1735
01:46:07.320 --> 01:46:08.720
Au Pak-man told me to plead guilty.

1736
01:46:09.600 --> 01:46:11.600
He said if I didn't. he would kill me.

1737
01:46:11.680 --> 01:46:12.920
Do you think this scares me?

1738
01:46:13.000 --> 01:46:15.240
Even if I have to go to prison.
I'll expose you.

1739
01:46:15.320 --> 01:46:16.640
Au Pak-man. you bastard.

1740
01:46:23.920 --> 01:46:27.200
Prosecutor. do you have
any further statements?

1741
01:46:41.600 --> 01:46:42.600
Ladies and gentlemen.

1742
01:46:46.960 --> 01:46:47.960
In Hong Kong.

1743
01:46:49.240 --> 01:46:50.680
the court values evidence above all.

1744
01:46:53.000 --> 01:46:54.240
However. sometimes

1745
01:46:55.440 --> 01:46:58.040
evidence does not guarantee
truth or justice.

1746
01:47:01.960 --> 01:47:03.720
Furthermore.

1747
01:47:04.320 --> 01:47:07.120
no judicial system is completely perfect.

1748
01:47:08.000 --> 01:47:11.440
Sometimes. loopholes may even appear.

1749
01:47:12.480 --> 01:47:13.680
These loopholes

1750
01:47:14.640 --> 01:47:16.280
are often exploited

1751
01:47:16.960 --> 01:47:20.080
by individuals with malicious intent.

1752
01:47:20.160 --> 01:47:22.240
It causes innocent people to suffer.

1753
01:47:22.320 --> 01:47:24.320
Just like the ongoing Ma Ka-kit case.

1754
01:47:26.520 --> 01:47:27.880
Just one wrongful judgment

1755
01:47:29.400 --> 01:47:31.800
can destroy an entire family.

1756
01:47:32.600 --> 01:47:34.320
That's why we. the judicial personnel.

1757
01:47:36.080 --> 01:47:39.520
will not allow any miscarriage of justice
under our watch.

1758
01:47:42.920 --> 01:47:45.680
We won't allow
miscarriages of justice on Ma Ka-kit.

1759
01:47:48.320 --> 01:47:50.040
We won't allow that

1760
01:47:51.640 --> 01:47:53.280
to happen to anyone.

1761
01:47:57.120 --> 01:48:00.000
This is our conscience
as legal personnel. Your Honor.

1762
01:48:08.720 --> 01:48:12.400
This court hereby pronounces the verdict.

1763
01:48:12.480 --> 01:48:15.600
The first defendant. Ma Ka-kit. is found
not guilty of drug trafficking charges

1764
01:48:15.680 --> 01:48:17.880
and is acquitted and released.

1765
01:48:35.520 --> 01:48:38.280
<i>The DOJ celebrates the fact</i>

1766
01:48:38.360 --> 01:48:40.176
<i>that the Ma Ka-kit case
has been successfully appealed.</i>

1767
01:48:40.200 --> 01:48:43.440
<i>The DOJ will continue to optimize
their performance.</i>

1768
01:48:43.520 --> 01:48:47.360
<i>enhancing the efficiency. quality.
and consistency of prosecution.</i>

1769
01:48:47.440 --> 01:48:51.120
<i>We'll also strengthen our cooperation
with other government departments</i>

1770
01:48:51.200 --> 01:48:54.440
<i>to provide high-quality legal services
to Hong Kong society.</i>

1771
01:48:54.520 --> 01:48:57.680
<i>ensuring fairness and justice
in the judicial process.</i>

1772
01:49:10.600 --> 01:49:13.840
AU PAK-MAN

1773
01:49:43.720 --> 01:49:45.616
You overturned your verdict
in the Ma Ka-kit case.

1774
01:49:45.640 --> 01:49:46.856
Does this suggest
that the justice system lacks fairness?

1775
01:49:46.880 --> 01:49:48.616
Could this have been
the result of human error?

1776
01:49:48.640 --> 01:49:49.640
That's right.

1777
01:49:50.520 --> 01:49:51.600
I admit

1778
01:49:51.680 --> 01:49:53.720
that the initial judgment

1779
01:49:53.800 --> 01:49:54.800
in this case

1780
01:49:55.600 --> 01:49:56.600
was indeed flawed.

1781
01:49:57.120 --> 01:50:01.120
This has raised doubts
and concerns among the public.

1782
01:50:01.200 --> 01:50:02.520
Regarding this matter.

1783
01:50:02.600 --> 01:50:04.600
I sincerely

1784
01:50:05.120 --> 01:50:07.800
regret and apologize.

1785
01:50:10.520 --> 01:50:14.360
QUALIFIED YOUTH PROGRAM TUITION
ASSISTANCE APPLICATION NOTICE

1786
01:50:21.880 --> 01:50:23.160
FOK CHI-HO

1787
01:50:23.240 --> 01:50:26.400
<i>Now. the case
has finally come to a clear conclusion.</i>

1788
01:50:26.480 --> 01:50:27.600
<i>The truth is revealed.</i>

1789
01:50:27.680 --> 01:50:30.880
